{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles","id":1543116,"title":"Lineages and Game Roles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-04T12:25:23-07:00","id":1543116,"title":"Lineages and Game Roles","content":"In White Wolf\u2019s older games crossovers were rare or difficult, though to the degree that it did or could happen, there were very distinct traditional game roles that were associated with different creature types. Werewolves would be the fighters, mages are weak but have high utility, vampires have more social oriented powers. Like D&amp;D classes in a sense - aside from a lack of balance and intention of crossover. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s pretty clear that Curseborne is the opposite in that they are intended to have different kinds of creatures in the same group. Presumably, with more balance (to the degree that it\u2019s possible) than WoD. <br /> <br /> Though, to finally get to my question, are certain lineages going to strongly define the roles of the characters? For example, will Primal characters be the front line fighters, will hungry be the social manipulators, will sorcerers be the glass cannon utility characters, etc?<br /> <br /> Or, could you for example, have a social primal character, a combat sorcerer, a utility hungry, a sneaky outcast, and so on?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T13:48:53-07:00","id":1543121,"title":"","content":"Gonna need the rest of the Lineages full writeups before we can get into the weeds of the discussion, but assumedly it's designed in similar fashion to Chronicles fashion, where the Families give you particular roles you can play as a single Family game, but the Lineages also have strong enough biases that you could also do it as a multi-Lineage game Like, there's a lot of reason why the Primal might be a very go to as your Hitter, but the Furies are decently well specced to also be the Hitter, stuff like that, in similar vain (from Chronicles) to how a Rahu Forsaken is top tier Hitter material, but an Elemental Lost or a Vengeful Sin-Eater still aren't Hitters to sneeze at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-04-2024, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T18:45:20-07:00","id":1543131,"title":"","content":"The different lineages and families will have different strengths and weaknesses, certainly, like primal as a major path might give (for example) 5 physical, 3 mental and 2 social attributes, but you can chose not to take lineage as your primary path and reduce it to 2/1/1 and instead take a more social family as your primary path if you want to get more social attribute points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T14:29:26-07:00","id":1543637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543131#post1543131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The different lineages and families will have different strengths and weaknesses, certainly, like primal as a major path might give (for example) 5 physical, 3 mental and 2 social attributes, but you can chose not to take lineage as your primary path and reduce it to 2/1/1 and instead take a more social family as your primary path if you want to get more social attribute points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now we've seen the actual numbers, it might be *intended* to work this way but it doesn't. <br /> <br /> Because Family and Lineage go together, Family locks in your Attributes very strongly. For all Outcasts and 4/7 Hungry your Attribute distribution is the same no matter which Path you make Primary. For the Dead, switching moves 1-2 points between Social and the other categories. For the Hungry it only ever moves one point, and sometimes moves it in unintuitive ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T16:16:50-07:00","id":1543645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543637#post1543637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now we've seen the actual numbers, it might be *intended* to work this way but it doesn't.<br /> <br /> Because Family and Lineage go together, Family locks in your Attributes very strongly. For all Outcasts and 4/7 Hungry your Attribute distribution is the same no matter which Path you make Primary. For the Dead, switching moves 1-2 points between Social and the other categories. For the Hungry it only ever moves one point, and sometimes moves it in unintuitive ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you claim it doesn't work that way, then complain that it does work that way but not to the degree that you wanted it to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T17:12:59-07:00","id":1543651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543645#post1543645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you claim it doesn't work that way, then complain that it does work that way but not to the degree that you wanted it to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I had a reply to this but it got flagged as spam because I made too many edits (I should proofread better). Let me try again.<br /> <br /> It depends on what you mean by &quot;work that way&quot;.<br /> <br /> Your choice of Family absolutely affects your Attribute spread, so yes if your Lineage is physically focused but your Family is Mental focused, for example, you'll get a mental focused character. In that sense, yes, it works that way.<br /> <br /> What *doesn't* affect it (and let's be clear I don't mean &quot;doesn't affect it as much as I'd like&quot; I mean &quot;literally does not affect it at all in any way&quot;) in 10 out of the 19 cases we've seen so far is which Path you flagged as Major.<br /> <br /> Try actually making an Outcast character and adding up your Attributes with Lineage Major, and then with Family Major. They'll come out the same every single time. Try it with every Hungry except an Heir, Bathorite or Vorare and it'll be the same. And if you try it with a Bathorite, you'll find that even though Hungry is a &quot;social&quot; Lineage and Bathorite is a &quot;physical&quot; Family, switching from Lineage-Major to Family-Major actually swaps one point from Physical to Mental.<br /> <br /> You can still cover the social/physical/mental bases within one Lineage, but more than 50% of families are completely locked into their distributions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T19:27:25-07:00","id":1543656,"title":"","content":"Yeah, now that I have seen some minor and major paths, I have to agree with Nobody Special. The path system, as it is now, doesn\u2019t give a lot of families much versatility. I see what they were going for, but I think it would be fun if I could make a highly physical, mental, or social character in the same family. <br /> <br /> If for example, I make a Chimera character, it will have 6 mental, 4 physical, and 4 social regardless of minor or major oath. That is a design failure, especially when it applies to so many families. Maybe it could be argued that <i>all Chimera </i>should be mentally focused and mediocre physically and socially - but if that is the intent why have minor and major paths at all? The obvious goal was to create some (ostensibly thematically) limited versatility in attribute distribution but that goal is not achieved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T19:41:44-07:00","id":1543659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543656#post1543656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, now that I have seen some minor and major paths, I have to agree with Nobody Special. The path system, as it is now, doesn\u2019t give a lot of families much versatility. I see what they were going for, but I think it would be fun if I could make a highly physical, mental, or social character in the same family.<br /> <br /> If for example, I make a Chimera character, it will have 6 mental, 4 physical, and 4 social regardless of minor or major oath. That is a design failure, especially when it applies to so many families. Maybe it could be argued that <i>all Chimera </i>should be mentally focused and mediocre physically and socially - but if that is the intent why have minor and major paths at all? The obvious goal was to create some (ostensibly thematically) limited versatility in attribute distribution but that goal is not achieved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do have a theory about how this happened. <br /> <br /> Warning, it gets mathsy.<br /> <br /> The mistake the designers seem to have made is to think what matters for Major and Minor paths is how big the numbers are, but that's actually not important because they'll always add up to 14 anyway.<br /> <br /> What matters is the *skew*. How big the *difference* between the categories is. <br /> <br /> Every time the choice of Major path made no difference, it was because for both paths, the Minor track was just 2 / 2 / 2 lower than the Major track. So whichever you made Minor, the skew stayed the same (all that happened was that you got 2 points of each category that *nominally* came from a different Path).<br /> <br /> To make it work as we can assume it's intended the Minor Path has to be *less skewed* than the Major Path (with the Bathorites the Minor Path is actually *more* skewed). Although even then I question how wield it is to have a system where you pick two sets of three numbers and then add them up in pairs when the outcome would be the same as just giving you one set of numbers and letting you add one or two points to it. <br /> <br /> Now I will say that in terms of customisation we haven't seen Roles yet but they should be an extra 4 points, which should help *a bit* but if they're locked to 1 / 1 / 2 (which I fear they might be) then aydin that would only really be one point you get to place freely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T20:50:33-07:00","id":1543665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543659#post1543659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do have a theory about how this happened.<br /> <br /> Warning, it gets mathsy.<br /> <br /> The mistake the designers seem to have made is to think what matters for Major and Minor paths is how big the numbers are, but that's actually not important because they'll always add up to 14 anyway.<br /> <br /> What matters is the *skew*. How big the *difference* between the categories is.<br /> <br /> Every time the choice of Major path made no difference, it was because for both paths, the Minor track was just 2 / 2 / 2 lower than the Major track. So whichever you made Minor, the skew stayed the same (all that happened was that you got 2 points of each category that *nominally* came from a different Path).<br /> <br /> To make it work as we can assume it's intended the Minor Path has to be *less skewed* than the Major Path (with the Bathorites the Minor Path is actually *more* skewed). Although even then I question how wield it is to have a system where you pick two sets of three numbers and then add them up in pairs when the outcome would be the same as just giving you one set of numbers and letting you add one or two points to it.<br /> <br /> Now I will say that in terms of customisation we haven't seen Roles yet but they should be an extra 4 points, which should help *a bit* but if they're locked to 1 / 1 / 2 (which I fear they might be) then aydin that would only really be one point you get to place freely.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re absolutely right, you\u2019ve figured out the math behind it. Almost all the lineage and family minor and major paths are only different by 2/2/2. In most cases, picking between lineage and family as major only determines where that extra 2/2/2 comes from but doesn\u2019t affect your actual attributes.<br /> <br /> This is a major flaw in the system as it now exists, making minor and major paths useless.<br /> <br /> If I were going to tweak it, I would skew he minor and major paths differently. Each one could represent a different thing that the family or lineage could potentially be good at.<br /> <br /> Here are some theoretically changed examples:<br /> <br /> <b>Outcast</b><br /> Major Path: Mental 3, Physical 4, Social 3<br /> Minor Path: Mental 1, Physical 1, Social 2<br /> <br /> <b>Chimera</b><br /> Major Path: Mental 5, Physical 2, Social 3<br /> Minor Path: Mental 1, Physical 3<br /> <br /> <b>Munificents</b><br /> Major Path: Mental 3, Physical 3, Social 4<br /> Minor Path: Mental 2, Social 2<br /> <br /> <br /> So with this set up, you could have the following:<br /> <br /> Chimera (lineage major, family minor)<br /> Mental 4, Physical 7, Social 3<br /> <br /> Chimera (lineage minor, family major)<br /> Mental 6, Physical 3, Social 5<br /> <br /> Munificent (lineage major, family minor)<br /> Mental 5, Physical 4, Social 5<br /> <br /> Munificent (lineage minor, family major)<br /> Mental 4, Physical 4, Social 6<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T01:58:38-07:00","id":1543671,"title":"","content":"Your Role Path adds further Attribute dots creating more variables, and that's introduced in the character creation chapter.<br /> <br /> Please feel free to submit your concerns via errata however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T05:00:24-07:00","id":1543674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543671#post1543671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Role Path adds further Attribute dots creating more variables, and that's introduced in the character creation chapter.<br /> <br /> Please feel free to submit your concerns via errata however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have done, and I'm aware role paths make a difference, I even mentioned that in my post. But this *cannot* be intentional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T05:27:11-07:00","id":1543676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I were going to tweak it, I would skew he minor and major paths differently. Each one could represent a different thing that the family or lineage could potentially be good at<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That was my first thought but even that has problems because you get a system transparency issue. Major vs Minor feels like it should mean &quot;most important vs least important&quot; but if you give them strong skews in different directions they become, as you say, two different, equally impactful options for character building.<br /> <br /> I think the only way to make it work as it feels it should work intuitively is to make sure every Minor path is 1 1 2 and every major path is at least 2 3 5, that way you're definitely making that Path pull in the direction it feels like it should but also making it pull that way less strongly when selected as Minor.<br /> <br /> An even simpler option would be to just say every stat pool starts at 4, then each Minor path adds 1 points to one stat and your Major path adds 4 points in some fixed distribution. That would be functionally what the current system seems to be going for but far more transparent. <br /> <br /> Or they could decouple Attributes from Paths entirely but then Paths only affect Inheritance (and honestly I gel like you should get both of those as well).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T18:41:05-07:00","id":1543720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543671#post1543671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Role Path adds further Attribute dots creating more variables, and that's introduced in the character creation chapter.<br /> <br /> Please feel free to submit your concerns via errata however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright. I\u2019ll do that.<br /> <br /> I am glad that the Role Path adds more customizability. As Nobody Special said, it does seem pretty certain that the issue they identified was unintentional so I think it\u2019s good to bring up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543676#post1543676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was my first thought but even that has problems because you get a system transparency issue. Major vs Minor feels like it should mean &quot;most important vs least important&quot; but if you give them strong skews in different directions they become, as you say, two different, equally impactful options for character building.<br /> <br /> I think the only way to make it work as it feels it should work intuitively is to make sure every Minor path is 1 1 2 and every major path is at least 2 3 5, that way you're definitely making that Path pull in the direction it feels like it should but also making it pull that way less strongly when selected as Minor.<br /> <br /> An even simpler option would be to just say every stat pool starts at 4, then each Minor path adds 1 points to one stat and your Major path adds 4 points in some fixed distribution. That would be functionally what the current system seems to be going for but far more transparent.<br /> <br /> Or they could decouple Attributes from Paths entirely but then Paths only affect Inheritance (and honestly I gel like you should get both of those as well).</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel a bit conflicted, because I kinda like my idea of choosing between two different kinds of focus for a certain family and how minor and major paths could mechanically handle that. In the other hand, what you say is right that it undermines the intention of the idea of lineage and family paths.<br /> <br /> Though lineage and family paths might themselves be a little self defeating because if you\u2019re in a certain family, you must be in the associated lineage. It\u2019s not something that be mixed and matched, like a Ahroun gives high Rage and a Lupus gives high Gnosis, so an Ahroun Lupus as high Rage and high Gnosis.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of starting with 3 across the board and then adding 1 or a distribution of 4 for minor and major paths.<br /> <br /> How might that look for Outcasts<br /> <br /> <b>Outcast Lineage</b><br /> Major: Mental 1, Physical 2, Social 1<br /> Minor: Physical 1<br /> <br /> The above pattern cannot be repeated for the families, or we end up with the same problem as before.<br /> <br /> <b>Battleground Angels</b><br /> Major: Mental 1, Physical 3<br /> Minor: Physical 1<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 4, Physical 6, Social 4<br /> Family Major: Mental 4, Physical 7, Social 3<br /> <br /> <b>Chimerae</b><br /> Major: Mental 3, Physical 1<br /> Minor: Mental 1\u200b<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 5, Physical 5, Social 4<br /> Family Major: Mental 6, Physical 5, Social 3<br /> \u200b<br /> <b>Nephilim</b><br /> Major: Mental 2, Social 2<br /> Minor: Mental 1\u200b<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 5, Physical 5, Social 4<br /> Family Major: Mental 5, Physical 4, Social 5<br /> <br /> <b>Keepers the Broken Vine</b><br /> Major: Mental 3, Social 1<br /> Minor: Mental 1\u200b<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 5, Physical 5, Social 4<br /> Family Major: Mental 6, Physical 4, Social 4<br /> <br /> <b>Munificents</b><br /> Major: Physical 1, Social 3<br /> Minor: Social 1\u200b<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 4, Physical 5, Social 5<br /> Family Major: Mental 3, Physical 5, Social 6<br /> <br /> <b>League of the Hidden Crossroad</b><br /> Major: Mental 1, Social 3<br /> Minor: Social 1\u200b<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 4, Physical 5, Social 5<br /> Family Major: Mental 4, Physical 4, Social 6<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> The families can\u2019t have +1, +1,+2 for a major path or we get the same problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T05:38:38-07:00","id":1543745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543720#post1543720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though lineage and family paths might themselves be a little self defeating because if you\u2019re in a certain family, you must be in the associated lineage. It\u2019s not something that be mixed and matched, like a Ahroun gives high Rage and a Lupus gives high Gnosis, so an Ahroun Lupus as high Rage and high Gnosis.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah one of the things I'm most concerned about is that the game ultimately seems to use Paths because that's Storypath's &quot;thing&quot;, not necessarily because it's well suited to the actual game. <br /> <br /> The three path Storypath system seems to hinge on the fact that you can take any three paths you want and gives you a lot of leeway to determine what those Paths are and mean. <br /> <br /> in They Came From, for example, Attributes are assigned independently of Paths and Path Skills are only suggestions. Most player abilities are chosen completely freely. And that's in a game that's *all about* playing one dimensional clich\u00e9d archetypes.<br /> <br /> The elephant on the room here is that Curseborne is constrained by the assumptions of Storypath Ultra. Which means if Paths determining Attributes and locking skills is in Ultra, it has to be in Curseborne even though it's in don't ways uniquely unsuited to it.<br /> <br /> I think it's also worth pointing out that in some ways lack of *customisation* isn't my concern. My real concerns are lack of transparency and unnecessarily complexity.<br /> <br /> By far the worst thing about the current Outcast situation, IMO, is that players are currently required to add up three pairs of numbers, which will likely be written in different pages, in order to get a result that's fixed. <br /> <br /> It's like if instead of VtM saying &quot;sign 7 points to your Primary category&quot; It said &quot;assign a number of points to your Primary category determined by adding the two numbers from the left hand column on the table at the bottom of this page&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T10:15:18-07:00","id":1543764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543745#post1543745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah one of the things I'm most concerned about is that the game ultimately seems to use Paths because that's Storypath's &quot;thing&quot;, not necessarily because it's well suited to the actual game.<br /> <br /> The three path Storypath system seems to hinge on the fact that you can take any three paths you want and gives you a lot of leeway to determine what those Paths are and mean.<br /> <br /> in They Came From, for example, Attributes are assigned independently of Paths and Path Skills are only suggestions. Most player abilities are chosen completely freely. And that's in a game that's *all about* playing one dimensional clich\u00e9d archetypes.<br /> <br /> The elephant on the room here is that Curseborne is constrained by the assumptions of Storypath Ultra. Which means if Paths determining Attributes and locking skills is in Ultra, it has to be in Curseborne even though it's in don't ways uniquely unsuited to it.<br /> <br /> I think it's also worth pointing out that in some ways lack of *customisation* isn't my concern. My real concerns are lack of transparency and unnecessarily complexity.<br /> <br /> By far the worst thing about the current Outcast situation, IMO, is that players are currently required to add up three pairs of numbers, which will likely be written in different pages, in order to get a result that's fixed.<br /> <br /> It's like if instead of VtM saying &quot;sign 7 points to your Primary category&quot; It said &quot;assign a number of points to your Primary category determined by adding the two numbers from the left hand column on the table at the bottom of this page&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, I agree. It seems like it is a system that doesn't quite support the game it's for. It is also, as you say, overly complicated and not transparent. Paths make the most sense when you can mix and match paths, when you can't (like in this case where all Outcast families automatically are in the Outcast lineage) then it doesn't quite work as well. Now, I personally do support more flexibility and customization, but greater transparency would at least make that lack of customization obvious so that it could be more easily identified and evaluated.<br /> <br /> I think that my revised rules above are better, in that they are both more customizable and therefore more transparent. It's still not as transparent or simplified as it could be without the Path system. I wouldn't expect them to remove the Path system, which isn't that bad, but it wouldn't be hard to tweak the bonuses so that minor and major path selection changes attribute distribution.<br /> <br /> I can apply similar rules to the Hungry and Dead:<br /> <br /> <b>Hungry Paths</b><br /> Major: Mental 1, Physical 1, Social 2<br /> Minor: Social 1<br /> <br /> <b>Ascetics</b><br /> Major: Mental 3, Social 1<br /> Minor: Mental 1\u200b<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 5, Physical 3, Social 6<br /> Family Major: Mental 7, Physical 3, Social 4<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>The Black Hearts</b><br /> \u200bMajor: Physical 2, Social 2<br /> Minor: Social 1<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 4, Physical 4, Social 6<br /> Family Major: Mental 3, Physical 5, Social 6<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<b>Gaki</b><br /> \u200bMajor: Mental 3, Physical 1<br /> Minor: Mental 1<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 5, Physical 4, Social 5<br /> Family Major: Mental 6, Physical 4, Social 4<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Heirs</b><br /> \u200bMajor: Mental 1, Social 3<br /> Minor: Social 1<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 4, Physical 4, Social 6<br /> Family Major: Mental 4, Physical 3, Social 7\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<b>House Bathory</b><br /> \u200bMajor: Physical 2, Social 2<br /> Minor: Physical 1<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 4, Physical 5, Social 5<br /> Family Major: Mental 3, Physical 5, Social 6\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Iscariots</b><br /> \u200bMajor: Physical 3, Social 1<br /> Minor: Physical 1<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 4, Physical 5, Social 5<br /> Family Major: Mental 3, Physical 6, Social 5<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Vorare</b><br /> \u200bMajor: Mental 1, Physical 3<br /> Minor: Physical 1<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 4, Physical 5, Social 5<br /> Family Major: Mental 4, Physical 6, Social 4\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <b>Dead Paths</b><br /> Major: Mental 1, Social 3<br /> Minor: Social 1\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Furies</b><br /> Major: Mental 1, Physical 3<br /> Minor: Physical 1\u200b<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 4, Physical 4, Social 6<br /> Family Major: Mental 4, Physical 6, Social 4<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Mavens</b><br /> \u200bMajor: Social 4<br /> Minor: Social 1<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 4, Physical 3, Social 7<br /> Family Major: Mental 3, Physical 3, Social 8<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<b>Poltergeists</b><br /> \u200bMajor: Mental 3, Social 1<br /> Minor: Mental 1<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 5, Physical 3, Social 6<br /> Family Major: Mental 6, Physical 3, Social 5\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Shades</b><br /> \u200bMajor: Mental 1, Physical 1, Social 2<br /> Minor: Social 1<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 4, Physical 3, Social 7<br /> Family Major: Mental 4, Physical 4, Social 6<br /> <br /> <b>Wardens</b><br /> \u200bMajor: Mental 2, Social 2<br /> Minor: Social 1<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 4, Physical 3, Social 7<br /> Family Major: Mental 5, Physical 3, Social 6\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Zeds</b><br /> \u200bMajor: Mental 2, Physical 2<br /> Minor: Physical 1<br /> Lineage Major: Mental 4, Physical 4, Social 6<br /> Family Major: Mental 5, Physical 5, Social 4\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T11:05:25-07:00","id":1543769,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it I wonder if part of the disconnect I'm having with the system here is that it depends a lot on whether the expected approach to character creation is:<br /> <br /> 1) Decide on the kind of character you rang to make<br /> 2) Pick a Lineage and Family that fits that character<br /> <br /> In which case the system is super flexible, or:<br /> <br /> 1) Decide which Family most appeals to you aesthetically, thematically or just in terms of what kewel powerz they have<br /> 2) Build a character that represents your take on our reaction against that family<br /> <br /> In which case it feels much more constrained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T12:00:02-07:00","id":1543776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543769#post1543769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about it I wonder if part of the disconnect I'm having with the system here is that it depends a lot on whether the expected approach to character creation is:<br /> <br /> 1) Decide on the kind of character you rang to make<br /> 2) Pick a Lineage and Family that fits that character<br /> <br /> In which case the system is super flexible, or:<br /> <br /> 1) Decide which Family most appeals to you aesthetically, thematically or just in terms of what kewel powerz they have<br /> 2) Build a character that represents your take on our reaction against that family<br /> <br /> In which case it feels much more constrained.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting point. I suppose I was coming at character creation from the second perspective. I think that the path system leads one to at least partly view things from the second perspective, since it suggests that there is supposed to be variation within families and not merely between them.<br /> <br /> The family is an affiliation as much as it is a power set. If we played a 19th century war based game, someone could make a character who is a British soldier. Saying that all British soldiers have primary physical, secondary mental, and tertiary social is limiting and reductivist. It would be better to have the option of making a brilliant tactician whose mental attributes are primary or a charming officer who can command men or woo women and has social attributes as primary. So too should a Keeper of the Broken Vine (which is an affiliation and power set, kind of like being a British solider is) have a number of options. Also, imagine in that 19th century game if multiple people want to be British soldiers, it would be a lot more interesting if you could have the smart one and the charming one in the group than just have them all be physically focused.<br /> <br /> Of course, Role Path does mitigate this issue, but aside from lack of transparency and being overly complicated (without benefit) it is a missed opportunity to have characters vary based on whether they identify more with their lineage or family - which is what the system suggests but fails to deliver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T16:23:05-07:00","id":1543791,"title":"","content":"So for what it's worth I've played around a bit assuming that Path Roles can go 0/0/4 (they can definitely go 0/1/3 because we see that in Ashcan characters) and that *does* make a big difference in customisability (although not I'd say in transparency or complexity). For a lot of families (although I've mostly looked at the Dead) you do have some customisability gains over a, say, 8/6/4 Primary/Secondary/Tertiary split.<br /> <br /> This system does allow you to be both more balanced (most Dead families can get a 6/6/6 split) and more skewed (some can go as far out as 3/3/12) but the Families that are capable of the wider swings also have some gaps. Mavens, for example, literally cannot have Physical higher than Social.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T16:41:19-07:00","id":1543799,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind characters will have another non-Lineage/Family plan which will presumably allow for 4 more Attribute dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T17:02:23-07:00","id":1543801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543799#post1543799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind characters will have another non-Lineage/Family plan which will presumably allow for 4 more Attribute dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I really honestly have taken this into account.<br /> <br /> Just so we're working from data here, assuming that Role Paths allow you to essentially put dots anywhere, here's what it looks like for the Dead:<br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Aptos Display\"><span style=\"color:#0f4761\">Dead</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Major: </b>3 / 2 / 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Minor:</b> 1 / 1 / 2</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Aptos Display\"><span style=\"color:#0f4761\">Furies</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Major: </b>3 / 5 / 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Minor:</b> 1 / 2 / 1</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Lineage Major Stats:</b> 4 / 4 / 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Family Major Stats:</b> 4 / 6 / 4</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Net effect: 2 points moved from Social to Physical. Character focus changes as a result.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Most Balanced Build: </b>6 / 6 / 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Strongest Physical Skew:</b> 4 / 10 / 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Strongest Mental Skew: </b>8 / 4 / 6 or 8 / 6 / 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Strongest Social Skew: </b>4 / 4 / 10</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Aptos Display\"><span style=\"color:#0f4761\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mavens</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Major: </b>2 / 2 / 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Minor:</b> 2 / 0 / 2</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Lineage Major Stats: </b>5 / 2 / 7</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Family Major Stats:</b> 3 / 3 / 8</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Net effect: two points moved from Mental, one into Physical, one into Social. Character gets more min-maxed.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Most Balanced Build:</b> 6 / 5 / 7 or 5 / 6 / 7</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Strongest Physical Skew: </b>3 / 7 / 8</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Strongest Mental Skew:</b> 9 / 2 / 7</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Strongest Social Skew:</b> 3 / 3 / 12</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Aptos Display\"><span style=\"color:#0f4761\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Poltergeists</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Major: </b>5 / 2 / 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Minor:</b> 2 / 1 / 1</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Lineage Major Stats:</b> 5 / 3 / 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Family Major Stats:</b> 6 / 3 / 5</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Net effect, one point moved from Social to Mental. Character focus changes as a result.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Most Balanced Build:</b> 6 / 6 / 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Strongest Physical Skew:</b> 5 / 7 / 6 or 6 / 7 / 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Strongest Mental Skew: </b>10 / 3 / 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Strongest Social Skew:</b> 5 / 3 / 10</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Aptos Display\"><span style=\"color:#0f4761\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Shades</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Major: </b>3 / 3 / 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Minor:</b> 1 / 1 / 2</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Lineage Major Stats:</b> 4 / 3 / 7</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Family Major Stats:</b> 4 / 4 / 6</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Net effect, one point moved from Social to Physical. Character gets less min-maxed.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Most Balanced Build:</b> 6 / 6 / 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Strongest Physical Skew:</b> 4 / 8 / 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Strongest Mental Skew:</b> 8 / 3 / 7 or 8 / 4 / 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Strongest Social Skew:</b> 4 / 3 / 11</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Aptos Display\"><span style=\"color:#0f4761\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Wardens</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Major: </b>4 / 2 / 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Minor:</b> 2 / 0 / 2</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Lineage Major Stats: </b>5 / 2 / 7</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Family Major Stats:</b> 5 / 3 / 6</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Net effect, one point moved from Social to Physical. Character gets less min-maxed.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Most Balanced Build:</b> 6 / 6 / 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Strongest Physical Skew:</b> 5 / 7 / 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Strongest Mental Skew:</b> 9 / 2 / 7 or 9 / 3 / 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Strongest Social Skew:</b> 5 / 2 / 11</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Aptos Display\"><span style=\"color:#0f4761\">Zeds</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Major: </b>4 / 4 / 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Minor:</b> 1 / 2 / 1</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Lineage Major Stats:</b> 4 / 4 / 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Family Major Stats:</b> 5 / 5 / 4</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Net effect, one point moved from Social to each other Attribute. Character focus changes from social primary to split physical/mental primary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Most Balanced Build:</b> 6 / 6 / 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Strongest Physical Skew:</b> 5 / 9 / 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Strongest Mental Skew:</b> 9 / 5 / 4</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Strongest Social Skew:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"> 4 / 4 / 10</span><br /> <hr /><br /> You have *reasonable* flexibility to pick your highest category, but at the cost of your lower categories being pretty much fixed. There are multiple Dead Families for example who pretty much can't go below a 6 in Social.<br /> <br /> I will say that flexibility-wise, I don't think this is necessarily worse <b>overall</b> than just having a Primary / Secondary / Tertiary split of, say, 8 / 6 / 4 (a distribution some families can happily emulate in most combinations anyway) but I think a lot of it comes back to what I said in my previous post.<br /> <br /> If you approach the game by saying &quot;I want to play a character with really good social skills&quot; and then look a the Lineages and Families and pick Maven, you're better off under this system because if you really want you can literally have 5 points in all your Social Attributes (<b>disclaimer</b> it might not work like this, there might be hard caps or 0/0/4 paths might not be a thing).<br /> <br /> If you approach the game by saying &quot;Hey, these Mavens look cool, I want to play an undead thrill-seeker&quot; then you might be a bit nonplussed to realise that you also need to be playing somebody highly charismatic, manipulative and composed none of which are actually qualities you might want in your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T19:53:58-07:00","id":1543814,"title":"","content":"With the Dead at least, combined with the 4 points from Role Paths, we have a fair amount of customizability. Certain families can\u2019t quite min-max in certain attribute categories, though they can be pretty good in a given category and all have the option of being balanced. <br /> <br /> Current rule Outcasts wouldn\u2019t be as good because they aren\u2019t different based on Major and Minor paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T05:36:41-07:00","id":1543855,"title":"","content":"Primal also have the 3/4/3 1/2/1 split same as Outcasts meaning a lot of Families again don't change distribution between Major and Minor.<br /> <br /> Having looked at the system in more detail I increasingly think Major and Minor Paths need to die in a fire, the customisability gains are just not worth the loss of transparency and simplicity.<br /> <br /> Especially because much as I complain about them not doing anything to Attributes, because they *also* set your Inheritance and your Inheritance can be central to the fantasy of the character you want to play sometimes that will guide your choice *anyway*. Like I'd always take Family primary for most Primal factions because so many of them bake in core parts of the were-x fantasy (why would I want to play a Vodnik who can't breathe underwater).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T07:48:24-07:00","id":1543857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543855#post1543855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primal also have the 3/4/3 1/2/1 split same as Outcasts meaning a lot of Families again don't change distribution between Major and Minor.<br /> <br /> Having looked at the system in more detail I increasingly think Major and Minor Paths need to die in a fire, the customisability gains are just not worth the loss of transparency and simplicity.<br /> <br /> Especially because much as I complain about them not doing anything to Attributes, because they *also* set your Inheritance and your Inheritance can be central to the fantasy of the character you want to play sometimes that will guide your choice *anyway*. Like I'd always take Family primary for most Primal factions because so many of them bake in core parts of the were-x fantasy (why would I want to play a Vodnik who can't breathe underwater).</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, which Primal families do you claim dont change because my quick glance through the document gave me the impression that they all do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T08:05:11-07:00","id":1543859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543857#post1543857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Out of curiosity, which Primal families do you claim dont change because my quick glance through the document gave me the impression that they all do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops, you're right it's not a many as I thought, just the 8 Hands and Hydes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T08:07:44-07:00","id":1543861,"title":"","content":"(Double replying to avoid the Edit bug)<br /> <br /> Although Vodnik have the unintuitive thing where if you go Lineage Major you get *less* physical bit more physical and your social stays the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T08:13:42-07:00","id":1543862,"title":"","content":"And what does having Spawn of Vodnik do for water breathing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T08:17:40-07:00","id":1543863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543862#post1543862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what does having Spawn of Vodnik do for water breathing?</div> </div> </div> </div>You get out as part of your Inheritance if it's Major but not if it isn't<br /> <br /> (Risking an edit since it's a new login)<br /> <br /> Also: Raptors got no change either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","user":"Nobody Special","date":". 10-15-2024, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T09:06:48-07:00","id":1543868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543863#post1543863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You get out as part of your Inheritance if it's Major but not if it isn't<br /> <br /> (Risking an edit since it's a new login)<br /> <br /> Also: Raptors got no change either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I missed that, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T09:07:09-07:00","id":1543869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543855#post1543855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primal also have the 3/4/3 1/2/1 split same as Outcasts meaning a lot of Families again don't change distribution between Major and Minor.<br /> <br /> Having looked at the system in more detail I increasingly think Major and Minor Paths need to die in a fire, the customisability gains are just not worth the loss of transparency and simplicity.<br /> <br /> Especially because much as I complain about them not doing anything to Attributes, because they *also* set your Inheritance and your Inheritance can be central to the fantasy of the character you want to play sometimes that will guide your choice *anyway*. Like I'd always take Family primary for most Primal factions because so many of them bake in core parts of the were-x fantasy (why would I want to play a Vodnik who can't breathe underwater).</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, they might be better off just going back to primary, secondary, and tertiary attribute categories chosen by the player regardless of lineage or family - just like WoD. That would increase transparency, customizability, and simplicity. It would only need to be mentioned once instead of big lists of numbers spread across numerous pages that players have to sort through when choosing a family and making a character. If you want to be a really social Get of Lyka or a really physical Maven, you can without difficulty, so good customization. It's completely transparent in its simplicity - you decide how relatively physical, mental, and social your character is - full stop. What you see is what you get.<br /> <br /> Of course, they aren't going to do that, because they want to stick with the path system. It is something that could be easily house ruled though. 8/6/4 would work perfectly fine. Or for greater flexibility but still limiting min-maxing, distribute 18 points but you have to put at least 3 and at most 9. As for inheritances, I think getting both would be cool, or if having only one is important to people then they can choose one and it doesn't affect attribute distributions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T09:26:48-07:00","id":1543871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543869#post1543869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, they aren't going to do that, because they want to stick with the path system.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not reason of Storypath system. <b>Scion, Trinity</b> and <b>They Came From </b>do not have those kinds of limits on Attritbutes. You just get limits from Paths on Skills. It's <b>Storypath ULTRA</b> rule - i.e. 2E of SP engine - check <b>Storypath Ultra Core Manual </b>on those rules. We are seeing first game on it, and so we have this system is itself too limited. <br /> <br /> I really do not know why devs are forcing this 'Paths gives you Attributes' approach in <b>Curseborne</b>, really. \ud83e\udd37\u200d\u2642\ufe0f","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T09:48:59-07:00","id":1543879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543871#post1543871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not reason of Storypath system. <b>Scion, Trinity</b> and <b>They Came From </b>do not have those kinds of limits on Attritbutes. You just get limits from Paths on Skills. It's <b>Storypath ULTRA</b> rule - i.e. 2E of SP engine - check <b>Storypath Ultra Core Manual </b>on those rules. We are seeing first game on it, and so we have this system is itself too limited.<br /> <br /> I really do not know why devs are forcing this 'Paths gives you Attributes' approach in <b>Curseborne</b>, really. \ud83e\udd37\u200d\u2642\ufe0f</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaah so it *is* a SPU rule. <br /> <br /> That explains a lot. It also means we're officially stuck with it. <br /> <br /> I do think it makes more sense in some games, those beung the ones where you can mix and match any part with any other path, and in some ways it *is* nice not to be locked to 8/6/4 or whatever because sometimes a different split makes sense. <br /> <br /> It's just that right now *so* much is bundled into Legacy and Family and the Major Path thing feels very much like a band aid solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T11:19:15-07:00","id":1543893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543879#post1543879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aaaah so it *is* a SPU rule.<br /> <br /> That explains a lot. It also means we're officially stuck with it.<br /> <br /> I do think it makes more sense in some games, those beung the ones where you can mix and match any part with any other path, and in some ways it *is* nice not to be locked to 8/6/4 or whatever because sometimes a different split makes sense.<br /> <br /> It's just that right now *so* much is bundled into Legacy and Family and the Major Path thing feels very much like a band aid solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could go with just 18 points to distribute. That is ultimate flexibility. If you want to limit min-maxing, limit it to a maximum of 9 and minimum of 3. This could include 9/6/3 or 6/6/6 or 7/7/4 or any number of other combinations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T14:43:33-07:00","id":1543910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543893#post1543893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They could go with just 18 points to distribute. That is ultimate flexibility. If you want to limit min-maxing, limit it to a maximum of 9 and minimum of 3. This could include 9/6/3 or 6/6/6 or 7/7/4 or any number of other combinations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that could also work although to be fair they could have used that system on any one of these games over the last 35 years so I won't fault them for not there.<br /> <br /> And the reality seems to be (assuming wyrdhamster has seen the manuscript) that Attributes from Paths is baked into SPU and the devs have been very clear that SPU systems are fixed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T16:37:32-07:00","id":1543925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543910#post1543910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the reality seems to be (assuming wyrdhamster has seen the manuscript) that Attributes from Paths is baked into SPU and the devs have been very clear that SPU systems are fixed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I literally checked my backers preview of <b>SPU Core Manual </b>before posting this<b>.</b> '<i>Attribites from Major &amp; Minor Paths'</i> is exactly from it quote, from chapter 1.<br /> <br /> I can only give you simple house rule to commit that - just 'move 1 dot from basic Arena divided numbers. For example if your Major Path gives you Mental 3, Physical 5 and Social 2 - you can modyfiy it to 2, 6, 2; 4, 4, 2 or 2, 5, 3, for example.' <br /> <br /> It's all I can just advice you to do with that system. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ( And yes, Attributes destitution hard backed into each Path I find VERY annoying, on both players side - but also as game designer. Imagine need to write ALL the game Paths with those spreads. I literally have cold shiver when thinking about my Transformers fan game writing for those 30+ Paths those needless complicated Attributes packages. \ud83d\ude1f<br /> <br /> It will also be a large nightmare for all 45 Paths of TC Assassins games.<br /> <br /> Bad, needless step here, Onyx Path. \ud83d\ude25 )<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T17:11:33-07:00","id":1543928,"title":"","content":"What method of attribute distribution would y\u2019all prefer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T17:58:34-07:00","id":1543936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543925#post1543925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I literally checked my backers preview of <b>SPU Core Manual </b>before posting this<b>.</b> '<i>Attribites from Major &amp; Minor Paths'</i> is exactly from it quote, from chapter 1.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry wasn't questioning your information just honestly hadn't remembered if you'd said you'd seen it or not. <br /> <br /> A bit disappointing that the Major/Minor path thing is built in as well. <br /> <br /> As for what I'd prefer, I'd be fine with free assignment but see why they don't want too use that. I think I'd go for a hybrid: do 7 / 5 / 3 distribution then have each Path give you a free door somewhere suitable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T18:56:49-07:00","id":1543939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543936#post1543936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for what I'd prefer, I'd be fine with free assignment but see why they don't want too use that. I think I'd go for a hybrid: do 7 / 5 / 3 distribution then have each Path give you a free door somewhere suitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be fine with that as well. I would also be fine with 18 to spend freely or 8/6/4. I think that my issue is with the major and minor family and lineage paths. <br /> <br /> What you mentioned about customization - thinking of a character abilities and then finding a family to match it - does seem reasonable one one level. Then again, let\u2019s say that you want a really mentally focused character who is also pretty strong and athletic and you don\u2019t want him to be particularly social. With the lineage and family paths, you\u2019re going to have to look through lists of dozens of different numbers trying to find something along the lines of what you\u2019re looking for, potentially having a conflict with the concept and the family attributes that match that concept. Comparing that to just putting 8 in mental, 6 in physical, and 4 in social makes it seem so convoluted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T22:10:21-07:00","id":1543950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543939#post1543939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would be fine with that as well. I would also be fine with 18 to spend freely or 8/6/4. I think that my issue is with the major and minor family and lineage paths.<br /> <br /> What you mentioned about customization - thinking of a character abilities and then finding a family to match it - does seem reasonable one one level. Then again, let\u2019s say that you want a really mentally focused character who is also pretty strong and athletic and you don\u2019t want him to be particularly social. With the lineage and family paths, you\u2019re going to have to look through lists of dozens of different numbers trying to find something along the lines of what you\u2019re looking for, potentially having a conflict with the concept and the family attributes that match that concept. Comparing that to just putting 8 in mental, 6 in physical, and 4 in social makes it seem so convoluted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dozens? Really? I set out to test your theory, I opened the most recent doc and decided to see how many families I had to search through to find a family like you suggested. It was literally the first family. <br /> <br /> I don't disagree that this method of doing attributes is inherently limiting, but let's keep it in perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T22:37:17-07:00","id":1543951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543950#post1543950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dozens? Really? I set out to test your theory, I opened the most recent doc and decided to see how many families I had to search through to find a family like you suggested. It was literally the first family.<br /> <br /> I don't disagree that this method of doing attributes is inherently limiting, but let's keep it in perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I guess you got lucky with that one, or I got unlucky. Though that assumes that you will immediately pick the werespider character without any desire to see more options. Also, even just looking at the first family that you pick, you\u2019re still looking at a dozen numbers - six from the lineage and six from the family. If you look at multiple families, then you get into the dozens of numbers. Also, what if you want a character that isn\u2019t a werespider? <br /> <br /> Not that this issue in the end of the world or anything, I\u2019m still excited for Curseborne. I wouldn\u2019t fret too much about an issue that can be fixed with one brief sentence of house rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T03:52:28-07:00","id":1543970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543950#post1543950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dozens? Really? I set out to test your theory, I opened the most recent doc and decided to see how many families I had to search through to find a family like you suggested. It was literally the first family.<br /> <br /> I don't disagree that this method of doing attributes is inherently limiting, but let's keep it in perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I agree we should keep this in perspective although in Sgt Brother's defend they did say dozens of numbers rather than dozens of splats.<br /> <br /> Spotting what a Family is meant to be good at is *fairly* intuitive as is spotting what a Lineage is meant to be good at. &quot;Mentally focused but strong and athletic, not particularly social&quot; is pretty easy to fulfil in Primal, for example because they're all slightly Physical tilted from Family. It's harder to fulfil in Dead (You can do do it with the first family you try but Furies and Zeds are basically your only option).<br /> <br /> Where it gets tricky is when that doesn't actually track onto stats in the way you expect, especially how the Major / Minor thing currently works.<br /> <br /> The single biggest problem for me from a customization perspective is that it it's notably hard to play against type, something the framing of the game almost directly encourages you to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T05:12:17-07:00","id":1543974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543951#post1543951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I guess you got lucky with that one, or I got unlucky. Though that assumes that you will immediately pick the werespider character without any desire to see more options. Also, even just looking at the first family that you pick, you\u2019re still looking at a dozen numbers - six from the lineage and six from the family. If you look at multiple families, then you get into the dozens of numbers. Also, what if you want a character that isn\u2019t a werespider?<br /> <br /> Not that this issue in the end of the world or anything, I\u2019m still excited for Curseborne. I wouldn\u2019t fret too much about an issue that can be fixed with one brief sentence of house rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you familiar with the term &quot;moving the goalposts&quot;? This is a textbook case of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T05:22:37-07:00","id":1543976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543970#post1543970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The single biggest problem for me from a customization perspective is that it it's notably hard to play against type, something the framing of the game almost directly encourages you to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and no. It's fairly difficult to get less than a 3 in an attribute category, and you can take a role that grants you +3. That means in all but the most extreme cases you can have 6 points in an attribute spread, that's enough to max one attribute and keep the others at average. The only time you have difficulty playing against the type is when you specifically set your type as something that requires a large number of attribute dots. <br /> <br /> Compare this to D&amp;D where it's also hard to play something against the type, like say a wizard who wears full armor and fights with a sword. Both systems can do it, you just won't be as good at it as people who fit into their intended roles as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T06:39:02-07:00","id":1543980,"title":"","content":"I think you might be misconstruing what I mean by &quot;play against type&quot; and are being *slightly* overgenerous to the system in interpreting 6 in a spread as enough to really qualify as a focus. Sure you can max out one attribute but as you say that locks the others to being merely average. <br /> <br /> I think that's fine-ish for Mental because Intelligence, Cunning and Resolve (I believe those are the SPU terms) don't really go together that closely so there's a reasonable chance you might want to play somebody who is street smart but not book smart or very resolute but not otherwise &quot;clever&quot; in any sense.<br /> <br /> I'd say it falls below minimum for the Social and Physical spheres. Most physical or social archetypes kind of need a 4/3/3 spread to sell the fantasy. Most athletes for example, evening college level athletes, need notable amounts of both strength, dexterity, and stamina, ideally with an emphasis on the one that's most useful for their sport. Combat wombats need all three and again ideally an emphasis on their particular style so your bruisers don't look the same as your dex monkeys.<br /> <br /> The other thing I'd say is that for me &quot;playing against type&quot; means what you're bad at as well as what you're good at. It's currently impossible to create a Hyde, Ascetic or Chimera, for example without 6 points in Mental. But one of the major themes of the game is that you often *don't* get to choose your Family. I shouldn't have to fit on with my smart, cunning, resolute peers.<br /> <br /> basically the way I see it, 3 points in a spread is bog standard, 6 is notably above average but not great, 9 is excellent. I don't need any given splat to be able to go to a 3 or a 9 in every attribute but I do think a good rule of thumb is that they should always be able to go above and below 6.<br /> <br /> As for the D&amp;D comparison. Firstly, these are very different types of game. If you play a Wizard in D&amp;D you are ultimately choosing to play a character who does wizard stuff. By comparison if I choose to play a Lycan in Curseborne I could mean to play all kinds of things. I could want to be a frontline combat monster or I could want to be a cunning but cowardly fox shifter, or a prom queen who hates being a Werewolf. <br /> <br /> On top of which, D&amp;D actually does let me put my Attribute points wherever I'd like even if it's not optimal for my class. If I want to build a wizard who wears armour and gifts with a sword and isn't especially smart I not only *can do that* but I will be about as good at fighting with a sword as most low level characters. Most importantly, I will be better at fighting with a sword than most town guards and bandits so by the standards of the world, my sword wizard actually works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T09:55:52-07:00","id":1543997,"title":"","content":"I wasn't trying to move the goalpost. When I said dozens of numbers, I was referring to a dozen numbers that you have to look at for each family (6 for the family and 6 for the lineage) and then add together the attribute from both minor/major path selections - often to see that they are the same.<br /> <br /> Even if this provides adequate customization, it is so much more complicated and cumbersome than old fashioned primary, secondary, and tertiary attribute categories chosen by the player. <br /> <br /> As time goes by D&amp;D has made it easier to play against type. If you go back to 1st or 2nd edition AD&amp;D, then its a little bit hard to play a close combat wizard. It can still be done though, even with higher physical attributes than Intelligence, even if its not optimal. As it moved on to 3rd and eventually 5th edition, it became easier to multiclass, get feats, take a special class or subclass or prestige class, or various other methods of making a character who primarily casts spells but can also fight. In V:tM, you could make a close combat Tremere or Malkavian character with primary physical attributes. You could make a social primary Nosferatu or Gangrel.<br /> <br /> I really don't see the advantage of the path system determining attributes in comparison to 8/6/4 or distribute 18. The only potential advantage that I see is making it harder to pay outside of type, which I don't think many people see that has a benefit including the authors from what I can gather.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T11:02:13-07:00","id":1543999,"title":"","content":"Under Storypath, the Attributes part of character creation is where I\u2019ve seen most people struggle between how arenas and favored approach works. While I\u2019ve only create a few characters using Storypath Ultra (and one was At the Gates where Major path is decided for you), it feels a bit easier to understand for new players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T12:35:48-07:00","id":1544011,"title":"","content":"Personally, Zak, that was always the easiest part for my players. It was intuitive.<br /> <br /> But, the major problem with the Path system and Curseborne is that you are forced to take Lineage and Family as 2 of the 3 Paths and the lack of variety in them is where the issues come up. I think that if they did not have the Families and Lineage be 2 of your Paths and maybe rework things to you only had to take a Lineage, that you could possibly have more variety in your makeup. Want to play a Fury that is a front liner? Sure. Instead, want your Fury to be a scheming type who takes her revenge by ruining people socially or even politically or professionally? Then take the appropriate Major Path to do so and let the Dead/Fury be a Minor Path. <br /> <br /> I suppose maybe giving us five or six Path choices under each Lineage rather than a Lineage AND a Family may work better to allow for more change up on what to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T15:53:04-07:00","id":1544029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543980#post1543980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you might be misconstruing what I mean by &quot;play against type&quot; and are being *slightly* overgenerous to the system in interpreting 6 in a spread as enough to really qualify as a focus. Sure you can max out one attribute but as you say that locks the others to being merely average.<br /> <br /> I think that's fine-ish for Mental because Intelligence, Cunning and Resolve (I believe those are the SPU terms) don't really go together that closely so there's a reasonable chance you might want to play somebody who is street smart but not book smart or very resolute but not otherwise &quot;clever&quot; in any sense.<br /> <br /> I'd say it falls below minimum for the Social and Physical spheres. Most physical or social archetypes kind of need a 4/3/3 spread to sell the fantasy. Most athletes for example, evening college level athletes, need notable amounts of both strength, dexterity, and stamina, ideally with an emphasis on the one that's most useful for their sport. Combat wombats need all three and again ideally an emphasis on their particular style so your bruisers don't look the same as your dex monkeys.<br /> <br /> The other thing I'd say is that for me &quot;playing against type&quot; means what you're bad at as well as what you're good at. It's currently impossible to create a Hyde, Ascetic or Chimera, for example without 6 points in Mental. But one of the major themes of the game is that you often *don't* get to choose your Family. I shouldn't have to fit on with my smart, cunning, resolute peers.<br /> <br /> basically the way I see it, 3 points in a spread is bog standard, 6 is notably above average but not great, 9 is excellent. I don't need any given splat to be able to go to a 3 or a 9 in every attribute but I do think a good rule of thumb is that they should always be able to go above and below 6.<br /> <br /> As for the D&amp;D comparison. Firstly, these are very different types of game. If you play a Wizard in D&amp;D you are ultimately choosing to play a character who does wizard stuff. By comparison if I choose to play a Lycan in Curseborne I could mean to play all kinds of things. I could want to be a frontline combat monster or I could want to be a cunning but cowardly fox shifter, or a prom queen who hates being a Werewolf.<br /> <br /> On top of which, D&amp;D actually does let me put my Attribute points wherever I'd like even if it's not optimal for my class. If I want to build a wizard who wears armour and gifts with a sword and isn't especially smart I not only *can do that* but I will be about as good at fighting with a sword as most low level characters. Most importantly, I will be better at fighting with a sword than most town guards and bandits so by the standards of the world, my sword wizard actually works.</div> </div> </div> </div>3 is significantly above average. I can guarantee you if you saw the stats of every IRL athlete you'd see 2s and 3s far more often than 4s and 5s. So yes, I do think 5 in one stat while average in the other 2, or above average in all 3 is plenty to consider yourself good in a category. <br /> <br /> Now our of curiosity, outside of an entirely arbitrary &quot;I want a certain number of dogs in a certain place&quot; what do you think you can't play? Prom Queen who hates being a werewolf? Sure you can do that. Cunning but cowardly fox shifter? Yup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T16:05:37-07:00","id":1544030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1543997#post1543997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't trying to move the goalpost. When I said dozens of numbers, I was referring to a dozen numbers that you have to look at for each family (6 for the family and 6 for the lineage) and then add together the attribute from both minor/major path selections - often to see that they are the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet after I pointed out that your example was possible on the very first family I looked at your immediate response was to try and dismiss it for reasons outside of your initial parameters, ie. Your comment complaining that it's a werespider. <br /> <br /> Regardless, I didn't have to look at &quot;dozens of numbers&quot;. I didn't have to look at a dozen numbers, the first 6 are sufficient, regardless of which path I choose as major. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if this provides adequate customization, it is so much more complicated and cumbersome than old fashioned primary, secondary, and tertiary attribute categories chosen by the player. </div> </div> </div>Maybe... But having character sheets at all is more complicated than just having everyone just say what their characters can do and automatically succeeding at everything. Complexity is not something to be avoided at all costs, it's to be judged on whether or not it adds to the game. <br /> <br /> That said, I can direct you to a character creation video by a well known content creator for Chronicles of Darkness content that got the basic attributes wrong for Scion so clearly the rules there were not perfectly clear and simple either. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As time goes by D&amp;D has made it easier to play against type. If you go back to 1st or 2nd edition AD&amp;D, then its a little bit hard to play a close combat wizard. It can still be done though, even with higher physical attributes than Intelligence, even if its not optimal. As it moved on to 3rd and eventually 5th edition, it became easier to multiclass, get feats, take a special class or subclass or prestige class, or various other methods of making a character who primarily casts spells but can also fight. In V:tM, you could make a close combat Tremere or Malkavian character with primary physical attributes. You could make a social primary Nosferatu or Gangrel.<br /> <br /> I really don't see the advantage of the path system determining attributes in comparison to 8/6/4 or distribute 18. The only potential advantage that I see is making it harder to pay outside of type, which I don't think many people see that has a benefit including the authors from what I can gather. </div> </div> </div>Tell me, other than &quot;I can't have an arbitrary number of dots where I want them&quot; what can you not play with the current rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T17:16:12-07:00","id":1544035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544029#post1544029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now our of curiosity, outside of an entirely arbitrary &quot;I want a certain number of dogs in a certain place&quot; what do you think you can't play? Prom Queen who hates being a werewolf? Sure you can do that. Cunning but cowardly fox shifter? Yup.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem here is you're begging the question. If you start from the premise that it's &quot;arbirtary&quot; to want particular dots in particular places then yes I fully agree that there's nothing I can't make with the current system because dots don't matter. But by that reasoning we don't need variable stats at all, we just give everybody 3 in everything and say it means whatever it's convenient for it to mean for that character.<br /> <br /> Like if you're right that the average professional athlete has 2s and 3s in their physical stats then the whole system for character creation is *totally* screwed because it means the average starting PC has the physique of a professional athlete, the mind of a career academic and the social skills of a seasoned con artist.<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> But let's actually work through the examples. <br /> <br /> Let's say I want to play a cuning but cowardly fox shifter.<br /> <br /> I take Get, Lineage Major, so I have 4 6 4<br /> <br /> I take a 2 0 2 Path to get to 6 6 6 (0 0 4 paths may not be a thing anyway and I probably want balanced stats).<br /> <br /> In the Mental space I take Intellect 3, Cunning 4, Resolve 2; physically I take Might 2, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3; Socially I take Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3.<br /> <br /> That's... fine but it's not really a statline that I think aligns well with what I'm going for. Sure you can *say* it's what I wanted but there's a lot about the statline that just looks blah. I could take a 1 0 3 path and go for Resolve 1 and Manipulation 4 but I was aiming for cowardly, not completely feckless. Ideally I'd take a point out of Physical but I can't do that because all Get are Physical 6.<br /> <br /> I appreciate that this is what you call &quot;arbitrary&quot; but it's actually very much not. To me it's very important that the numbers tell a story about what features of your character are important. Being highly dextrous isn't important to the character, but I'm locked into Dex being one of my highest Attributes. I could drop to 3 3 3 physicals but then the implosion is that being strong is as important to the concept as being smart.<br /> <br /> I appreciate that part of this is probably just being used to the old way of doing things but to me it's important that this *feels* like a Physical Tertiary character. Like it actually says something about what my priorities are as a player.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","user":"Nobody Special","date":". 10-16-2024, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T19:02:05-07:00","id":1544056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544035#post1544035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem here is you're begging the question. If you start from the premise that it's &quot;arbirtary&quot; to want particular dots in particular places then yes I fully agree that there's nothing I can't make with the current system because dots don't matter. But by that reasoning we don't need variable stats at all, we just give everybody 3 in everything and say it means whatever it's convenient for it to mean for that character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny, that's a lot of words to avoid answering the question. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like if you're right that the average professional athlete has 2s and 3s in their physical stats then the whole system for character creation is *totally* screwed because it means the average starting PC has the physique of a professional athlete, the mind of a career academic and the social skills of a seasoned con artist. </div> </div> </div>It's interesting that it went from &quot;athletes, even college&quot; to &quot;professional athletes&quot;. But yeah, a lot of athletes are average to above average physically, there's a skill that covers athletics and a 2 in a skill is, historically, sufficient to be a professional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T22:17:12-07:00","id":1544076,"title":"","content":"You can certainly create a wide range of characters, at least with regard to attribute distribution. They may not necessarily be the family that you want.<br /> <br /> But what do we gain from all of the complexity and the dozens of numbers? It seems like just being able to distribute points as you like is superior in every regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T04:21:47-07:00","id":1544083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544076#post1544076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can certainly create a wide range of characters, at least with regard to attribute distribution. They may not necessarily be the family that you want.<br /> <br /> But what do we gain from all of the complexity and the dozens of numbers? It seems like just being able to distribute points as you like is superior in every regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Flavor. You know a member of the Get will be physically powerful as the stereotype indicates they are. Now if having stereotypes be based on fact is in fact good, I'm not certain. <br /> <br /> Balance. I think 10/6/2 is the most uneven spread you can force, as opposed to 12/6/0 with distribution. I think this is probably worth something, but it's not exactly a lot with it being 2 attributes. <br /> <br /> Story shaping reality. The current rules enforce that both what you are and who you are influenced what you can do. If you're the whimpiest person in the world and are cursed into the Get of Lyla your body is going to change one way or another. Your pathes matter and help shape who your character is. <br /> <br /> Are those things worth it? I'm unsure. Despite it seeming like I'm defending the system, I'm not sold on it either. I'm currently learning Scion though and I will say your choice of Path seems way less impactful when it's just &quot;pick 3 skills.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T05:54:18-07:00","id":1544089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544056#post1544056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Funny, that's a lot of words to avoid answering the question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I answered the question, I just didn't give an answer you like. <br /> <br /> I completely agree that if you don't care where your points go, it doesn't matter how points are distributed and you can therefore make any character.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's interesting that it went from &quot;athletes, even college&quot; to &quot;professional athletes&quot;. But yeah, a lot of athletes are average to above average physically, there's a skill that covers athletics and a 2 in a skill is, historically, sufficient to be a professional. </div> </div> </div>What does &quot;Historically sufficient to be a professional&quot; mean?<br /> <br /> I consider myself to be distinctly *average* in all Physical categories. Plenty of people are less dextrous, mighty and full of stamina than I am. <br /> <br /> Literally any athlete, yes even college level, is sufficiently better than me in all of those areas that I would expect it to be reflected game mechanically.<br /> <br /> Or if that doesn't move the needle, try this. <br /> <br /> The Curseborne Ashcan gives regular cops six dice in their &quot;major&quot; pool, covering &quot;Arrest&quot;, &quot;Foot Chase&quot;, &quot;Car Chase&quot; and &quot;Marksmanship&quot;.<br /> <br /> That translates into 3 / 3 in Attribute and Skill, which means if rang to create an *average beat cop* as a PC I'm going to be at least 3 in Might and Dexterity plus penalty 3 in Close Combat and Ranged Combat as well.<br /> <br /> According to your interpretation those are well above professional levels of competence, what you'd expect from SWAT guys or trained military snipers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T06:29:30-07:00","id":1544092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544089#post1544089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does &quot;Historically sufficient to be a professional&quot; mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Storytelling system 2 dots of a skill is &quot;professional&quot; level and sufficient to earn a living. I think that applies to storypath games, but I can't swear to it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I consider myself to be distinctly *average* in all Physical categories. Plenty of people are less dextrous, mighty and full of stamina than I am. <br /> <br /> Literally any athlete, yes even college level, is sufficiently better than me in all of those areas that I would expect it to be reflected game mechanically. </div> </div> </div>You don't think you can lift as much as any single tennis player or golfer? You can't move quicker than the slowest football player? You think you're not tougher than a cheer leader who has to be tiny because they're the top of the pyramid? Really? If that's the case I doubt you're as average as you think you are. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or if that doesn't move the needle, try this.<br /> <br /> The Curseborne Ashcan gives regular cops six dice in their &quot;major&quot; pool, covering &quot;Arrest&quot;, &quot;Foot Chase&quot;, &quot;Car Chase&quot; and &quot;Marksmanship&quot;.<br /> <br /> That translates into 3 / 3 in Attribute and Skill, which means if rang to create an *average beat cop* as a PC I'm going to be at least 3 in Might and Dexterity plus penalty 3 in Close Combat and Ranged Combat as well.<br /> <br /> According to your interpretation those are well above professional levels of competence, what you'd expect from SWAT guys or trained military snipers. </div> </div> </div>First, antagonists don't play by the same rules as players, don't try and act like they do. But let's look at your example, they have might 3 and dexterity 3. Okay, how many attribute points have they spent to get there? 4 right? Minimum from a family and lineage is 2 (I believe) and you can get up to 3 from your role, meaning you can equal or exceed the job you want while still having a normal person's stamina. <br /> <br /> Second, yes, elite forces are going to be more skilled, last I checked skills aren't attributes. However, I do concede that some jobs demand higher than &quot;above average&quot; requirements. Question though, what do you think if someone tries to do those jobs, in real life, but without having the necessary attributes? They either fail to get into the job at all, or they wash out, or they end up just bad at their job, right? Not every person is amazing at what they do. Just like not every athlete is peak of human performance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T06:31:04-07:00","id":1544093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544083#post1544083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are those things worth it? I'm unsure. Despite it seeming like I'm defending the system, I'm not sold on it either. I'm currently learning Scion though and I will say your choice of Path seems way less impactful when it's just &quot;pick 3 skills.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Equally, I should add that while it seems like I'm attacking the system I do see all of these advantages. But like you I'm on the fence about whether making all the stereotypes true is good (incidentally I'd point out that this is *exactly* what I mean by it being hard to play against type) and the balance gains are minimal relative to pure free distribution and an actual *loss* relative to a fixed 8 6 4.<br /> <br /> The unambiguous gain from this system is the feeling that Path has *some* impact but right now because of the way it's set up, that impact is very large and also extremely rigid, while also requiring the player to manually calculate a bunch of numbers that won't meaningfully be different regardless of your choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T06:54:32-07:00","id":1544094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544092#post1544092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Storytelling system 2 dots of a skill is &quot;professional&quot; level and sufficient to earn a living. I think that applies to storypath games, but I can't swear to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to double check too but I think this is where we're disconnecting. The books sometimes say a particular dot level represents a particular thing but it doesn't actually follow it through in NPC stats or the way the rules work in real life.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't think you can lift as much as any single tennis player or golfer? You can't move quicker than the slowest football player? You think you're not tougher than a cheer leader who has to be tiny because they're the top of the pyramid? Really? If that's the case I doubt you're as average as you think you are. </div> </div> </div>Not the question. The question is whether if my *broad, general abilities* were translated into game terms I'd give myself higher Might, Dexterity and Stamina than them. Could the average person beat up a tiny cheerleader? Probably but in game terms the tiny cheerleader should probably still have Might 3 and Stamina 3 because she needs to be able to succeed at this which are game mechanically rolled using Might as Stamina.<br /> <br /> Game stats are abstractions. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, antagonists don't play by the same rules as players, don't try and act like they do. But let's look at your example, they have might 3 and dexterity 3. Okay, how many attribute points have they spent to get there? 4 right? Minimum from a family and lineage is 2 (I believe) and you can get up to 3 from your role, meaning you can equal or exceed the job you want while still having a normal person's stamina. </div> </div> </div>Right, I wasn't claiming it was impossible to build an average beat cop in any Family. It was that a 3 3 3 or 3 3 2 Attribute split in physical was, under the rules assumptions of Curseborne &quot;average beat cop&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, yes, elite forces are going to be more skilled, last I checked skills aren't attributes. However, I do concede that some jobs demand higher than &quot;above average&quot; requirements. Question though, what do you think if someone tries to do those jobs, in real life, but without having the necessary attributes? They either fail to get into the job at all, or they wash out, or they end up just bad at their job, right? Not every person is amazing at what they do. Just like not every athlete is peak of human performance. </div> </div> </div>Right, not every person is amazing at what they do, but the provided game stats for average people doing what they do averagely is 6 dice.<br /> <br /> To match that level of performance (which again is average job performance), irrespective of what a the flavour text says, you need at least 3s in your core Attributes. That's sorry of my point, an athlete with 3 4 3 isn't &quot;peak human performance&quot; they're &quot;mildly better than the average beat cop&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T06:56:46-07:00","id":1544095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544035#post1544035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Edit]<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And of course there's a huge edit to an hours old post while I'm typing a reply on my phone so I miss it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But let's actually work through the examples.<br /> <br /> Let's say I want to play a cuning but cowardly fox shifter.<br /> <br /> I take Get, Lineage Major, so I have 4 6 4<br /> <br /> I take a 2 0 2 Path to get to 6 6 6 (0 0 4 paths may not be a thing anyway and I probably want balanced stats). </div> </div> </div>Ok, you want balanced stats. I bet you won't complain about having balanced stat within the next paragraph, right? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the Mental space I take Intellect 3, Cunning 4, Resolve 2; physically I take Might 2, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3; Socially I take Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3.<br /> <br /> That's... fine but it's not really a statline that I think aligns well with what I'm going for. Sure you can *say* it's what I wanted but there's a lot about the statline that just looks blah. I could take a 1 0 3 path and go for Resolve 1 and Manipulation 4 but I was aiming for cowardly, not completely feckless. Ideally I'd take a point out of Physical but I can't do that because all Get are Physical 6. </div> </div> </div>It took 2 paragraphs for you to complain about having the thing you said you wanted. <br /> <br /> But let's ignore that and let's discuss your actual concept and how the attributes work for it. Your first adjective is &quot;cunning.&quot; Interestingly enough cunning is an attribute and you have it at a high level, that's good. We can agree you've got that part of your character covered and move on. <br /> <br /> The other adjective you chose to describe your character is &quot;cowardly&quot;. How'd you do? Well let's look at what cowardly means. According to google, it's &quot;lacking courage.&quot; Unfortunately there's no single stat called courage in this system so we'll have to look at what other stats might cover courage. That's going to be Resolve and Composure. Your resolve is average and your composure (probably more of a courage stat than resolve) is above average. Seems you could drop 1 or both attributes down to below average and have 3 points to work with, although I will admit having both Resolve and Composure at 1 would probably be &quot;completely feckless&quot; so I'd keep one or the other at 2 at least. You still have enough points for the changes you said you wanted. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I appreciate that this is what you call &quot;arbitrary&quot; but it's actually very much not. To me it's very important that the numbers tell a story about what features of your character are important. Being highly dextrous isn't important to the character, but I'm locked into Dex being one of my highest Attributes. I could drop to 3 3 3 physicals but then the implosion is that being strong is as important to the concept as being smart. </div> </div> </div>Now see, this argument I somewhat agree with. It's a weakness of the current system. Where we disagree is in the severity of the problem and if the solutions are better. I also think you have a skewed view of what attribute numbers represent, but we'll have a better idea of how SPU and Curseborne in particular views the attributes <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I appreciate that part of this is probably just being used to the old way of doing things but to me it's important that this *feels* like a Physical Tertiary character. Like it actually says something about what my priorities are as a player.<br /> </div> </div> </div>I get what you're trying to say here, but I do want to point out that there's absolutely no connection between physical ability and courage or lack of physical ability and cowardice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T07:06:29-07:00","id":1544096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544094#post1544094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not the question. The question is whether if my *broad, general abilities* were translated into game terms I'd give myself higher Might, Dexterity and Stamina than them. Could the average person beat up a tiny cheerleader? Probably but in game terms the tiny cheerleader should probably still have Might 3 and Stamina 3 because she needs to be able to succeed at this which are game mechanically rolled using Might as Stamina.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... no. The cheerleader isn't rolling might alone, nor stamina. The Cheerleader is rolling a dice pool consisting of an attribute plus a skill. That skill is, in this case, probably athletics, and they probably have it at a fairly decent level. Keep in mind a dice pool of 4 is going to succeed significantly more often than it fails. Also, keep in mind that a failure doesn't mean they're falling and breaking a leg it could be as simple as a false start attempting to get atop the pyramid. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Right, I wasn't claiming it was impossible to build an average beat cop in any Family. It was that a 3 3 3 or 3 3 2 Attribute split in physical was, under the rules assumptions of Curseborne &quot;average beat cop&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Again, NPCs don't play by the same rules as PCs. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Right, not every person is amazing at what they do, but the provided game stats for average people doing what they do averagely is 6 dice. </div> </div> </div>No, in your example an &quot;average cop&quot; (who has both special requirements and special training for their job) doing what they do best is 6 dice. That's not at all the same thing as &quot;an average person doing what they do averagely is 6 dice.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To match that level of performance (which again is average job performance), irrespective of what a the flavour text says, you need at least 3s in your core Attributes. </div> </div> </div>You think it's impossible to get a dice pool of 6 without 3 in an attribute? You can have 1 in an attribute and still have a dice pool of 7 without getting into any supernatural abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T07:23:28-07:00","id":1544102,"title":"","content":"We're now replying to multiple posts by each other so I hope this isn't getting confusing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544095#post1544095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, you want balanced stats. I bet you won't complain about having balanced stat within the next paragraph, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I typed this I thought you'd pick me up on that. My goal here was to work through the process.<br /> <br /> I will say in advance though that I specifically *don't* want balanced stats, I want a mental/social focus. The closest I can get to that is an even split because of the way Lycans work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It took 2 paragraphs for you to complain about having the thing you said you wanted.<br /> <br /> But let's ignore that and let's discuss your actual concept and how the attributes work for it. Your first adjective is &quot;cunning.&quot; Interestingly enough cunning is an attribute and you have it at a high level, that's good. We can agree you've got that part of your character covered and move on.<br /> <br /> The other adjective you chose to describe your character is &quot;cowardly&quot;. How'd you do? Well let's look at what cowardly means. According to google, it's &quot;lacking courage.&quot; Unfortunately there's no single stat called courage in this system so we'll have to look at what other stats might cover courage. That's going to be Resolve and Composure. Your resolve is average and your composure (probably more of a courage stat than resolve) is above average. Seems you could drop 1 or both attributes down to below average and have 3 points to work with, although I will admit having both Resolve and Composure at 1 would probably be &quot;completely feckless&quot; so I'd keep one or the other at 2 at least. You still have enough points for the changes you said you wanted. </div> </div> </div>I mean I could do this but I have you my reasoning and it's my character so I kind of think I get final day in what stats feel right for me?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now see, this argument I somewhat agree with. It's a weakness of the current system. Where we disagree is in the severity of the problem and if the solutions are better. I also think you have a skewed view of what attribute numbers represent, but we'll have a better idea of how SPU and Curseborne in particular views the attributes </div> </div> </div>Okay so I think we're taking at cross purposes here. <br /> <br /> I don't think the lack of customisability is a major issue, I think the lack of transparency and literally pointless (as in legally achieving nothing) complexity is a major issue. <br /> <br /> in terms of a skewed idea of what Attributes represent, I've been having that debate for literally twenty years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get what you're trying to say here, but I do want to point out that there's absolutely no connection between physical ability and courage or lack of physical ability and cowardice. </div> </div> </div>Oh absolutely and that's legit, but similarly there isn't a strong link between cowardice and lack of resolve or composure. <br /> <br /> It wasn't intended as an example of a character you couldn't make at all, it was an example of why, contrast to D&amp;D, a character concept in CB doesn't let you safely make a bunch of mechanical assumptions about what they should be good at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T07:38:03-07:00","id":1544103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544096#post1544096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um... no. The cheerleader isn't rolling might alone, nor stamina. The Cheerleader is rolling a dice pool consisting of an attribute plus a skill. That skill is, in this case, probably athletics, and they probably have it at a fairly decent level. Keep in mind a dice pool of 4 is going to succeed significantly more often than it fails. Also, keep in mind that a failure doesn't mean they're falling and breaking a leg it could be as simple as a false start attempting to get atop the pyramid.</div> </div> </div> </div>A dice pool of *two* succeeds more often than it fails if you're only rolling against Difficulty 1.<br /> <br /> I think this is the heart of the disconnect.<br /> <br /> You seem to be looking at what the books (possibly not even the SPU books, possibly the CofD core rulebooks) say something represents and working from there. I'm looking at how it actually feels in a game.<br /> <br /> If a cheerleader, a good cheerleader, one who could actually cheerlead for a living, is Might 2 Athletics 2 while I'm Might 2 Athletics 1 (since I don't take zero exercise) that means they, on average, only get 0.4 more Hits than I do on cheerleading tasks. They have a 26% chance of failing outright to do might-based cheerleading tasks compared to my (with *no cheerleading experience*) 34%.<br /> <br /> A character with 2s in their physical stats and 2 dots in Athletics doesn't actually, in-game, feel athletic. They feel pretty mid. And it gets worse if difficulties go higher.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, NPCs don't play by the same rules as PCs. </div> </div> </div>They don't play by the same character creation rules, but a dice pool is a dice pool.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, in your example an &quot;average cop&quot; (who has both special requirements and special training for their job) doing what they do best is 6 dice. That's not at all the same thing as &quot;an average person doing what they do averagely is 6 dice.&quot; </div> </div> </div>But now you're suggesting that the special requirements and training of the average beat cop (which let's be real are not exactly stringent) require them to have dice pools of 6. So that's what we're aiming for.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You think it's impossible to get a dice pool of 6 without 3 in an attribute? You can have 1 in an attribute and still have a dice pool of 7 without getting into any supernatural abilities. </div> </div> </div>As far as I can tell in SPU nothing adds to dice pools directly (it adds Enhancements) so you need 1/5, 2/4, 3/3, 4/2 or 5/1.<br /> <br /> In fact to get a dice pool of six assuming you have &quot;professional level&quot; competence, which according to you is only 2 dice, you actually need an attribute of 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T07:43:27-07:00","id":1544106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544102#post1544102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh absolutely and that's legit, but similarly there isn't a strong link between cowardice and lack of resolve or composure.</div> </div> </div> </div>The definition of composure: the state or feeling of being calm and in control of <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?client=safari&amp;sca_esv=9665476702a22ff3&amp;rls=en&amp;sxsrf=ADLYWILRnT3CjWoH7gGCnDOI8rpNjSVJpg:1729176139595&amp;q=oneself&amp;si=ACC90nwUEXg6u2vxy-araGkF9MAx1UHQ6wuqhE6oLKAcl1Um5SSbhatnX0ZSYSjcEBjoqcAIfNI3uXyOTNVrJwPzNnTEfX6ox4rh5GJAgGNsdodJHF7i82Y%3D&amp;expnd=1&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjkzbeM05WJAxW8ENAFHbo_JAwQyecJegQIQBAO\" target=\"_blank\">oneself</a>. <br /> <br /> So ya, there's a strong link between cowardice and the lack of being calm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T07:47:54-07:00","id":1544107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544103#post1544103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A dice pool of *two* succeeds more often than it fails if you're only rolling against Difficulty 1.<br /> <br /> I think this is the heart of the disconnect.<br /> <br /> You seem to be looking at what the books (possibly not even the SPU books, possibly the CofD core rulebooks) say something represents and working from there. I'm looking at how it actually feels in a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you? How many games have you actually played your &quot;cunning cowardly fox shifter&quot; in with Curseborne ruleset? Be honest now, I want the exact number. How many have you played with the cheerleader? Because you seem to be claiming extensive experience in playing a game that won't be released for over another year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T07:47:59-07:00","id":1544108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544106#post1544106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The definition of composure: the state or feeling of being calm and in control of <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?client=safari&amp;sca_esv=9665476702a22ff3&amp;rls=en&amp;sxsrf=ADLYWILRnT3CjWoH7gGCnDOI8rpNjSVJpg:1729176139595&amp;q=oneself&amp;si=ACC90nwUEXg6u2vxy-araGkF9MAx1UHQ6wuqhE6oLKAcl1Um5SSbhatnX0ZSYSjcEBjoqcAIfNI3uXyOTNVrJwPzNnTEfX6ox4rh5GJAgGNsdodJHF7i82Y%3D&amp;expnd=1&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjkzbeM05WJAxW8ENAFHbo_JAwQyecJegQIQBAO\" target=\"_blank\">oneself</a>.<br /> <br /> So ya, there's a strong link between cowardice and the lack of being calm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly trying to assume you're engaging in good faith here but can we please not resort to argument from dictionary definitions.<br /> <br /> Cowardice is a personality trait. You can be a coward in a perfectly controlled way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T07:49:29-07:00","id":1544109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544108#post1544108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm honestly trying to assume you're engaging in good faith here but can we please not resort to argument from dictionary definitions.<br /> <br /> Cowardice is a personality trait. You can be a coward in a perfectly controlled way.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now I honestly believe you're just trolling. I kind of thought as much with your whole &quot;you're just using the books I'm speaking from experience&quot; argument, but this confirms it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T07:50:54-07:00","id":1544110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544107#post1544107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you? How many games have you actually played your &quot;cunning cowardly fox shifter&quot; in with Curseborne ruleset? Be honest now, I want the exact number. How many have you played with the cheerleader? Because you seem to be claiming extensive experience in playing a game that won't be released for over another year.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've played a ton of D10 based dicepool games, for 20 years. The core mechanics and dice probabilities are effectively the same.<br /> <br /> A character with four or five dice in the thing they're supposed to be really good at doesn't feel really good at it. That was true in VtM in the 90s and VtR in the 2010s and it's true today. It seems disingenous to pretend that they do. The game *itself* gives its baseline antagonists way more dice than that and those are the guys who are meant to be little more than speedbumps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T07:55:05-07:00","id":1544111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544109#post1544109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And now I honestly believe you're just trolling. I kind of thought as much with your whole &quot;you're just using the books I'm speaking from experience&quot; argument, but this confirms it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I expressed that badly. I wasn't intending to imply you weren't speaking from experience.<br /> <br /> But you seem to be interpreting Attribute scores by what the book says they represent. I'm not saying that doesn't mean you're familiar with this kind of game, *loads* of people interpret it that way. But I don't think it's helpful.<br /> <br /> The books have, and have always had, flavour text descriptions of what different levels of dots represent, but those descriptions have always borne little to no resemblance to the game mechanical effects those dots actually have.<br /> <br /> By the flavour text in the book, sure, somebody with Might 3 is *astronomically* better than somebody with Might 2. On the table, they succeed *slightly* more often. And that, to me, actually does matter for selling the fantasy of the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T08:20:25-07:00","id":1544113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544110#post1544110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character with four or five dice in the thing they're supposed to be really good at doesn't feel really good at it. That was true in VtM in the 90s and VtR in the 2010s and it's true today. It seems disingenous to pretend that they do. The game *itself* gives its baseline antagonists way more dice than that and those are the guys who are meant to be little more than speedbumps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing, the group you play with defines &quot;feel&quot; a lot more than dice do. Look at your cheerleader character for a moment. She's going to get atop the pyramid. What happens? <br /> <br /> One option is that she rolls her might plus athletics like you previously suggested. A second option is that she's not using might at all, maybe she's trying to dexterously climb the pyramid and is using dex plus athletics. Or maybe she's using cunning plus athletics. Hell, a different option is that she's not rolling by herself at all, it's a team work action because she's not getting to the top of the pyramid by herself. The rules can be used to support all of that, and thus enable the low might cheerleader that you insist doesn't exist. <br /> <br /> But also, what happens if she fails? Maybe she gets close to the top, falls and cracks her skull open and dies right there in front of everyone... but probably not. Most likely she just doesn't get to the top, she had a false start and seconds later she makes it to the top when she aces her second roll. If failure is extremely punishing low dice pools &quot;feel&quot; bad, but when it's a few seconds of a setback and not much more, then having a dice pool of 4 or 5 isn't the worst thing ever and it's okay to fail the occasional roll. <br /> <br /> That's not even getting into the whole &quot;you don't have to roll a pilot roll every time you sit behind a steering wheel&quot; argument. <br /> <br /> And that's across the whole ruleset. Your cop example doesn't use &quot;might&quot; to determine their dicepools, so to get a matching dice pool while doing the same thing as the cop maybe a PC approaching someone trying to make an arrest would need cunning instead of might, or maybe the pc is approaching it trying to wear the suspect down and needs resolve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T09:48:37-07:00","id":1544115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544083#post1544083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Flavor. You know a member of the Get will be physically powerful as the stereotype indicates they are. Now if having stereotypes be based on fact is in fact good, I'm not certain.<br /> <br /> Balance. I think 10/6/2 is the most uneven spread you can force, as opposed to 12/6/0 with distribution. I think this is probably worth something, but it's not exactly a lot with it being 2 attributes.<br /> <br /> Story shaping reality. The current rules enforce that both what you are and who you are influenced what you can do. If you're the whimpiest person in the world and are cursed into the Get of Lyla your body is going to change one way or another. Your pathes matter and help shape who your character is.<br /> <br /> Are those things worth it? I'm unsure. Despite it seeming like I'm defending the system, I'm not sold on it either. I'm currently learning Scion though and I will say your choice of Path seems way less impactful when it's just &quot;pick 3 skills.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes embracing stereotypes can be fun. Sometimes it can be fun to go against stereotype. The problem is forcing people at adhere to stereotypes. If someone wants to play a super physical viking combat monster Get of Lyka character, they can put their points into that. Then again, if they want to play a more social and cerebral Get character, they could do that as well with point distribution. Is it going to detract someone's fun if a player decides to make a werewolf character with only a few points in physical attributes? I don't think it would. It's not like free point distribution prevents anybody from playing into the stereotype if they like.<br /> <br /> As for balance, 10/6/2 is still pretty minmaxy though not as bad as 12/6/0. Then again, distribute 18 with at most 9 and at least 3 makes it even harder to minmax and allows for greater flexibility. 8/6/4 forces even more balance.<br /> <br /> The reality in a world can conform to certain trends without forcing those trends on players. I know that this issue isn't as politically charged gender based attribute modifications, but the idea of forcing stereotypes is similar. If someone says that in real life and in the reality of the game world, that men are stronger than women. For that to be a reality of the setting, does that mean that all characters have to adhere to that tendency? Tendencies, statistical averages, and true stereotypes can exist in the reality of a game setting (or the reality of the actual world for that matter) without forcing everybody to adhere to those stereotypes. Most Lykans can be very physical and still allow for players to be exceptions if they think that is cool.<br /> <br /> I don't think that those things are worth it, especially with all of the added complexity and reduced transparency of the current system when 18 or 8/6/4 are options. Though in a similar vein as you say, I don't hate this system or anything and I like to stay optimistic about it. I still think that Curseborne seems like a cool fun game even if I have an issue with a few of the mechanics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T09:56:29-07:00","id":1544117,"title":"","content":"On a tangential note, all role playing games have issues with attributes modeling reality. In D&amp;D the difference between an average person's Strength (10) and a huge brute (18) is +4 on a d20 roll. That means that frequently the average person will win in a feat of strength against the brute, where as in a realistic situation, there are numerous activities where the brute will always succeed at and the average person will always fail at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T10:58:11-07:00","id":1544121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544113#post1544113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's the thing, the group you play with defines &quot;feel&quot; a lot more than dice do. Look at your cheerleader character for a moment. She's going to get atop the pyramid. What happens?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cutting most of this just because I think so the quoting back and forth is only making the conversation hard to follow at this stage.<br /> <br /> This is a super valid point and I don't disagree in general but I think the way I'd rather put it is to say that the way you play affects *how* the system affects you, not that it's the dominant effect.<br /> <br /> For example, one of the things your suggest is using alternative dice pools and that's definitely a valid call but it's also kind of an indirect way of dealing with the issue. It's essentially solving the problem of low dice pools making your character feel less competent by just never rolling your low dice pools. That's valid but it has downsides, it encourages min-maxing and can make people who just accepted their characters being bad at some stuff feel cheated.<br /> <br /> Limited consequences for failure actually does make small dice pools feel less bad, but at the cost of making all dice rolls feel less consequential. It also directly cuts against the suggested play pattern of the game, which seems to be based around an &quot;only roll if there's significant risk of consequences&quot; model.<br /> <br /> More generally, the big disagreement here seems to be what level 3 in an Attribute represents. You seem (and again I'm not meaingto put words in your mouth) to be coming from the perspective that it represents being *massively* above average. Like Might 5 means you're a finalist in World's Strongest Man, Might 4 means you're an Olympic powerlifter and Might 3 means you're not Olympic level but you're still seriously jacked.<br /> <br /> This *is* how it's often been described down the years but the problem I've always had with that interpretation is that it basically bundles well over 90% of people and far more than 90% of people you might actuality be *playing* outside of some very unusual games into 2 dots. This is even worse in Curseborne because the game is explicitly street level. One of the signature PCs is basically an ordinary high school teen.<br /> <br /> I tend to view Attributes much more generation and much more relative to the individual PC. Putting a start at 5 isn't saying &quot;I'm literally the best person at this thing in the world&quot;, it's saying &quot;this is my thing, I would like to do well when I take this approach to stuff&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course as you say we haven't seen the whole system yet but we have seen the Ashcan and we do know that the devs chose to give the PCs enough points to have 3 dots in literally every Attribute. That at least *suggests* to me that they don't consider a 3 dot stat to be particularly remarkable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","user":"Nobody Special","date":". 10-17-2024, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T11:09:50-07:00","id":1544122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544117#post1544117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a tangential note, all role playing games have issues with attributes modeling reality. In D&amp;D the difference between an average person's Strength (10) and a huge brute (18) is +4 on a d20 roll. That means that frequently the average person will win in a feat of strength against the brute, where as in a realistic situation, there are numerous activities where the brute will always succeed at and the average person will always fail at.</div> </div> </div> </div>D&amp;D is an excellent example here because the difference between normal strength and brute is +4 on a D20 and the only reason this remotely works is that D&amp;D treats its Attributes extremely abstractly. Like it's completely possible for a gnome to have Strength 20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T13:52:29-07:00","id":1544137,"title":"","content":"Potential double post because my last one got flagged as spam for too many edits and there's no telling how quickly it'll be approved, if ever.<br /> <br /> OK, setting aside the petty name calling and childish behaviour, it really doesn't matter what attributes represent in real life terms, the original point of this thread still stands. Currently it seems like too many major/minor combinations end up being the same, or with just one or two points shifted around, making it pointless to distinguish between major and minor paths other than picking which inheritance you get. Playing a Sorcerer Archivist for example. Sorcerer is 4/3/3 or 2/1/1, and Archivist is 5/2/3 or 3/0/1. They look pretty different, but when added together they both add up to 7/3/4, so why even bother having the major/minor thing for attributes. I still like the idea of having a pool of points you can distribute amongst attributes, with certain minimums and maximums. Then Lineages and Families provide bonuses based on their stereotype. Lineages and Families can even provide bonuses to specific attributes rather than just mental, physical, social. Make it like in Requiem where each clan gets +1 to one of two different attributes. It's better than the false variation we have now when all the major/minor lineage/family values adding up to the same stat distribution anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T14:11:53-07:00","id":1544140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544137#post1544137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I still like the idea of having a pool of points you can distribute amongst attributes, with certain minimums and maximums. Then Lineages and Families provide bonuses based on their stereotype.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would probably be the best option, although honestly even just having the classic oWoD 7/5/3 then each Path giving you a +1 would keep a reasonable amount of transparency and allow for Path to affect Attributes to some extent.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately that's also kind of off the table as far as I can tell. Storypath Ultra seems (you'd need to check with somebody who's familiar with the core) to mandate three paths, one of them Major, each providing Attribute points in a particular array.<br /> <br /> [Risking an Edit]<br /> <br /> Just to highlight how much of a problem this is. As far as I can tell it's *only* amongst the Dead that the Major choice ever moves more than one Attribute point.<br /> <br /> To complete my list of which families change and which don't, for the Sorcerers:<ul><li>Archivists have no effect</li> <li>Faceless move one point from Physical to Social</li> <li>The Network moves one point from Social to Mental</li> <li>The Premiere moves one point from Social to Physical</li> <li>The Reeves move one point from Mental to Physical</li> <li>Unburdened move one point from Social to Mental.</li> </ul>And on the one hand, one point isn't nothing, but on the other hand, it often <i>literally is nothing</i>. If, as we're currently assuming, you can effectively assign your Role Path Attributes freely (I'll admit this is potentially a *very* awkward assumption, Role paths may be fixed and how much it's acceptable to just take a Role you don't intend to literally play just for the attributes will vary a lot from table to table) then the Major Path point movement only matters if you were intending put either zero points into the Attribute the dot was moved out of or maximum points into the Attribute it was moved into (or the other way around, if you chose not to move the dot).<br /> <br /> Even leaving the customisability issues aside (and I do think they're non trivial) this is just so much work for so little result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","user":"Nobody Special","date":". 10-17-2024, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T16:49:36-07:00","id":1544152,"title":"","content":"Isn't the basic issue just that Family determines Lineage? In SPU by-the-book each Path is independent of the others, and you make a PC that's skewed towards one attribute category by picking Paths that are all skewed that way. Curseborne has been designed to force PCs from the same Family to have the same distribution of attribute dots (apart from whatever the Role Paths do) so every Family has a stereotype, and none of its members stray far from it. Just as well that the book has 30 different Families in it.<br /> <br /> We haven't yet seen what happens if you make a Role Path major, by the way. Presumably that's how you make a PC who tries to avoid their curses and live a relatively mundane life.<br /> <br /> I feel that tying attribute distribution to Paths just complicates designing Paths, but that's a problem with building SPU <i>games,</i> not SPU characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T17:12:36-07:00","id":1544157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544152#post1544152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the basic issue just that Family determines Lineage?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are basically two problems. The first is that Family determines Lineage, the second is that a *lot* of Minor Paths are just the Major Path reduced by 2 across the board and if two of those paths come together you wind up with it not mattering which Path you make Major at all.<br /> <br /> Also we don't know for certain but it *seems* like you can't make a Role Path Major, certainly none of the sample PCs in the Ashcan have Role as a Major Path and it seems you have to have an Inheritance which you get from making either Lineage or Role your Major Path (you maybe *could* choose not to take one?).<br /> <br /> Lineage being tied to Path is what leads most strongly to the customisability issue, the impact of which varies a lot depending on how you think you're supposed to approach character creation.<br /> <br /> Major and Minor paths varying by 2/2/2 is a big contributor to the fact that choice of Major Path kinda does nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T22:02:06-07:00","id":1544180,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#c0392b\">Please refrain from double posting in an attempt to circumvent the spam tools. Also, please keep the discussion civil, and bear in mind the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\">forum rules</a> regarding conduct going forward. </span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T10:06:32-07:00","id":1544207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544121#post1544121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course as you say we haven't seen the whole system yet but we have seen the Ashcan and we do know that the devs chose to give the PCs enough points to have 3 dots in literally every Attribute. That at least *suggests* to me that they don't consider a 3 dot stat to be particularly remarkable.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a general rule, player characters are considered to be exceptional in almost every RPG ever. The accursed are exceptional just from being accursed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T00:44:15-07:00","id":1544266,"title":"","content":"You are quite correct. This isn't a game where your characters are supposed to be weaker than the average beat cop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T01:02:25-07:00","id":1544267,"title":"","content":"I remember back in the days of early V:tM they tied Strength to bench pressing ability. It was always a point of interest for me, since I played V:tM and lifted weights so when I got to certain weights, I would feel triumphant that if I were a V:tM character that I would have that higher Strength score. <br /> <br /> What I gather now is that the attributes are a bit more nebulously defined, which may be good in some ways and bad in others. <br /> <br /> By the standards I\u2019m more used to, of the older WoD games, I always thought that the typical cop would have mostly physical attributes of 2, with the occasional 3 in there. With usually 2 points in combat related abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T04:29:13-07:00","id":1544272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544266#post1544266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are quite correct. This isn't a game where your characters are supposed to be weaker than the average beat cop.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right but the question isn't &quot;are you supposed to be weaker than the average beat cop&quot; it's &quot;is the average beat cop supposed to be massively mightier, more dexterous and more enduring than the average person or are they meant to be kind of average for somebody with a moderately physical job who still may well eat a lot of donuts&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T04:33:46-07:00","id":1544274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544272#post1544272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right but the question isn't &quot;are you supposed to be weaker than the average beat cop&quot; it's &quot;is the average beat cop supposed to be massively mightier, more dexterous and more enduring than the average person or are they meant to be kind of average for somebody with a moderately physical job who still may well eat a lot of donuts&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting and kind of dishonest that you felt the need to include &quot;massively&quot; and to contrast them with someone else who might reasonably also have above average physical abilities. You're stacking your question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T05:25:28-07:00","id":1544279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544274#post1544274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting and kind of dishonest that you felt the need to include &quot;massively&quot; and to contrast them with someone else who might reasonably also have above average physical abilities. You're stacking your question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, my fault for not communicating clearly.<br /> <br /> I took Matthew's statement as confirming that yes, Might 3 is meant to be &quot;average beat cop&quot;. If the average beat cop had Might 2 his comment would feel like a non sequitur. So my question wasn't supposed to be a cute way of asking what physical stats a beat cop should have, so much as asking what those physical stats should be taken to represent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T06:04:47-07:00","id":1544280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544279#post1544279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, my fault for not communicating clearly.<br /> <br /> I took Matthew's statement as confirming that yes, Might 3 is meant to be &quot;average beat cop&quot;. If the average beat cop had Might 2 his comment would feel like a non sequitur. So my question wasn't supposed to be a cute way of asking what physical stats a beat cop should have, so much as asking what those physical stats should be taken to represent.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I misread what you wrote, that's on me. Sorry man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T06:25:50-07:00","id":1544282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544267#post1544267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember back in the days of early V:tM they tied Strength to bench pressing ability. It was always a point of interest for me, since I played V:tM and lifted weights so when I got to certain weights, I would feel triumphant that if I were a V:tM character that I would have that higher Strength score.<br /> <br /> What I gather now is that the attributes are a bit more nebulously defined, which may be good in some ways and bad in others.<br /> <br /> By the standards I\u2019m more used to, of the older WoD games, I always thought that the typical cop would have mostly physical attributes of 2, with the occasional 3 in there. With usually 2 points in combat related abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah there seems to be a move away from that because it implies a false level of simulation. Your Strength (now Might) doesn't actually determine how much you bench, it determines how many dice you roll on Strength tests. <br /> <br /> If you want really clear evidence that they've moved away from the concrete interpretation of Attributes and Skills look at Issy Plummer.<br /> <br /> Her statline, under the traditional approach, would be thrown back in the player's face for being min maxed.<br /> <br /> &quot;Carl,&quot; the ST would say &quot;your character is supposed to be a seventeen year old girl but you've given her 3 4 3 physicals and Close Combat 5. I'll let the Attributes slide because okay, she's a Werewolf and maybe there's some supernatural reason that even in human form she's way stronger and tougher than the average adult man and also as quick as an Olympic athlete, but why in the name of Gaia have you also made her the world's greatest kenjitsu master? What while other kids were smoking behind the bike sheds she was studying the sword?&quot;<br /> <br /> It seems a whole lot, from the way Issy's sheet is written, like she was designed to just ... be the combat character. Might 3 isn't about how much she can bench because that's not what the game is actually about of trying to model. It's about how many dice she gets to roll when doing Might stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T06:27:18-07:00","id":1544283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544280#post1544280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I misread what you wrote, that's on me. Sorry man.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah that's cool, it was less clear from context than I thought it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T07:00:57-07:00","id":1544287,"title":"","content":"They're not supposed to represent an exact value in any measurable quantity. They're an abstraction that assists you in passing or failing at a task.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T11:23:56-07:00","id":1544302,"title":"","content":"Character Attributes are not supposed to be measured against normal people. The Storyguide uses a completely different system for stats on characters they control for an important reason, and that's to divorce the idea that we are comparing our character's Attributes to real world physical measurements. We aren't doing that. The Attributes don't measure anything. They measure how <b>likely</b> it is that a character is going to succeed on an action using it. That's it. <br /> <br /> So, if you have Might 3, you have a decent chance of overcoming most strength related challenges. This isn't average. This is pretty extraordinary. Also, Attributes are not the primary driving factor of the fiction in Storypath games. Skills are. You must have a Skill to take an appropriate action. There is no &quot;roll with Attribute even if you don't have an appropriate Skill&quot; in Storypath. You first choose what Skill the action requires, then pair an Attribute. In a lot of cases, the choice of Attribute has nothing to do with the chosen Skill, and everything to do with how you're approaching the situation. Are you attacking someone's weak spot to maximize damage? Maybe make a case for using Cunning instead of Might. We normalized the attack Attributes in SPU because people were having a hard time wrapping their heads around this aspect of the game, but it's always been part of the design, and it shows up everywhere else.<br /> <br /> Antagonists have things they are good at, things they are just okay at, and things they suck at, which are represented by an entire dice pool for doing those things. They do not have Skills and Attributes the way characters do. Their pools are an abstraction of how good they are at those things, both because it's far easier for the SG to interpret and use, and to because they are almost always less bad-ass overall than characters, meaning we do not need to know every Attribute under every circumstance, we only need to know what they're best at, because otherwise they are probably kind of shit. This is important, because we want the characters players control to be good at a great many things, and have only a few weaknesses. Where NPCs are the other way around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Danielle Lauzon, Requiem Developer, Storypath Guru, freelance writer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious","name":"impernious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T13:07:48-07:00","id":1544306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impernious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544302#post1544302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Character Attributes are not supposed to be measured against normal people. The Storyguide uses a completely different system for stats on characters they control for an important reason, and that's to divorce the idea that we are comparing our character's Attributes to real world physical measurements. We aren't doing that. The Attributes don't measure anything. They measure how <b>likely</b> it is that a character is going to succeed on an action using it. That's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, that's pretty much how I've always interpreted it.<br /> <br /> But in some ways that makes the customisability issue with the current system more acute.<br /> <br /> If your Attributes are essentially a measure of your character's preferred or most-likely-to-succeed approach to difficult situations, then it's even more important that players have a significant degree of control over what their characters' attributes are. Even if a character's Intellect, Cunning and Resolve scores don't actually translate to a real-world IQ rating or its equivalent, playing a mental-primary character does strongly imply that your character prefers to think their way around problems rather than, say, talk their way out or fight their way out.<br /> <br /> As the system currently stands, there are multiple Families who have an Attribute group they can't take below 7 and several more who have one they can't take below 6 (I can't comment on maximums without knowing for sure how Role Paths work). This places real limits on the type of character you can play in those Families.<br /> <br /> I appreciate you want PCs to have a lot of strengths and few weaknesses, but some characters are locked out of putting their few weaknesses where they might want to. Right now you *basically* can't play a Maven who is bad at taking a Social approach, or a Battleground Angel who is bad at taking a Physical approach even if you want to. I suppose you could intensely min-max within the category but even then you're mathematically incapable of having more than one stat below 3 (a level you say yourself qualifies as &quot;extraordinary&quot;).<br /> <br /> This might be an intentional feature of the system, but right now from my perspective as a player who is genuinely excited for this game, it doesn't feel like one. I'm honestly not suggesting much (admittedly we've bandied around a lot of ideas on this thread but that's kinda what this thread is *for*), I just think the numbers need to be tweaked to the point that every family can get every Attribute group down to 5 (still very good, but possible to build weaknesses in) and up to 7 (enough that it feels like a specialisation and a preferred approach within that specialisation).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T13:47:15-07:00","id":1544309,"title":"","content":"On one hand, I see the point in such abstractions, but on the other hand imagining a character\u2019s real world abilities is part of the fun of role playing. A game of pure abstraction would be craps or roulette. You roll the dice for craps, you win or you lose, but there is no meaning behind the dice roll. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s fun to imagine that the numbers we see on a character sheet mean something that has real world significance that could be compared to real people and events. Could my character win in a fist fight against a professional MMA fighter? How much can they lift? How fast can they run? What is my character\u2019s IQ and their college GPA. Maybe not all of those questions are interesting to us, but real world comparison is the essence of role playing.<br /> <br /> Now, abstraction can be useful if it allows for multiple real world interpretations for the same attribute. For example, is a human with a Might of 5 a huge power lifter strongman type of person? Could a person with a Might of 5 be much weaker than that but who is so ferocious that they hit as hard as the strongman? I imagine that there are plenty of professional boxers who hit as hard or harder than competitive power lifters even though they are a lot weaker. Or should that be determined by close combat skill? Could you say that your character has an IQ of 160 even with an Intellect of 2, because they have trouble focusing that intellect into things that are captured by the dice rolls?<br /> <br /> From the high abstraction standpoint, it becomes even more desirable (as Nobody Special says) for flexibility within the system, since the themes associated with characters and families can potentially match with many of the interpretations of certain attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T18:00:18-07:00","id":1544330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544309#post1544309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On one hand, I see the point in such abstractions, but on the other hand imagining a character\u2019s real world abilities is part of the fun of role playing. A game of pure abstraction would be craps or roulette. You roll the dice for craps, you win or you lose, but there is no meaning behind the dice roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sympathise with this but I'm a *massive* stan for high abstraction systems in this context because they solve two of my biggest RPG bugbears: flavour text masquerading as rules, and false expectation.<br /> <br /> Like you, I did really *enjoy* the little straplines in classic White Wolf games. Phrases like &quot;you can juggle six knives blindfold&quot; and &quot;damn, I was aiming for his *left * nostril&quot; are seared into my brain and have been for literal decades.<br /> <br /> But the problem was that the descriptions didn't at all match what those dots did in the actual game. A Dex 5 character who tried to juggle six knives blindfold would be marginally more likely to succeed than a Dex 4 character, but if the ST said they needed five successes on difficulty nine, they'd probably both fail.<br /> <br /> Plus the system just, well, *was abstract*. Slightly less so than SPU but we're talking about a system that had one skill covering *all of science* and another covering all other academic subjects. Everything from sprinting to darts was &quot;athletics&quot; and melee weapons covered sport fencing and knife fights in gutters.<br /> <br /> Worse, people's desire to treat the system as (to use a phrase that was popular back in the day) &quot;the physics of the gameworld&quot; led to some weird arguments and some genuinely unhelpful taboos in the community. You got STs who would straight up refuse to let any player take more than 3 dots in any skill because if 5 was human maximum it stood to reason that you could only have it by being the literal best in the world and by the same logic to get a level 4 you'd need to be at least competitive at an international level. Never mind that these hypothetical world champions were never going to appear in your game or interact with your characters. <br /> <br /> And the advantage of the abstract approach you've pretty much identified. You can more honestly reflect the range of things those stats can represent and, more importantly, what they will actually be used for in a game. You don't have to insist that every character with Might 5 be a circus strongman or Olympic weightlifter, or that every character with a high Intelligence have a &quot;genius level IQ&quot;. That isn't actually helpful unless your game revolves heavily around lifting dumbells and doing IQ tests.<br /> <br /> And it's not like the abstract system isn't grounded in any sense of game reality at all. In some ways it's actually *more* grounded in it because it doesn't claim to do things it doesn't. Besides, abstract doesn't mean arbitrary. Having high Might does still mean something concrete, it's just that what it means isn't &quot;you can bench this amount&quot;, it's &quot;you are good at achieving your goals using physical force&quot;.<br /> <br /> Issy's character sheet from the Ashcan is a great example of how this approach can be good. The fact she has Might 3 Close Combat 5 isn't meaningless, it means she's very good in a fight. It just isn't also trying to mean that she truly has mastered every known armed and unarmed martial art because that's not the sort of thing the game is trying to simulate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T19:03:24-07:00","id":1544333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impernious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543116-lineages-and-game-roles?p=1544302#post1544302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Attributes are not the primary driving factor of the fiction in Storypath games. Skills are. You must have a Skill to take an appropriate action. There is no &quot;roll with Attribute even if you don't have an appropriate Skill&quot; in Storypath. You first choose what Skill the action requires, then pair an Attribute.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, can I also clarify what you mean by this. What does &quot;you must have a Skill to take an appropriate action&quot; mean? Do you just mean that all actions must be have an associated skill or do you literally mean that you cannot attempt an action if you do not have at least one dot in the skill? Like are you actually saying that if you don't have at least one dot in Persuasion you can never try to persuade anybody of anything?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}